    this exact kind of check passed a 4-line stub (the coloringbook drill). Nothing in
    the backlog re-tests the verifier once built -- build once, trust forever, and
    you've reproduced the founding failure one level up.
    
    docs/agents/RED_TEAM_VERIFICATION.md exists but is a DIFFERENT thing -- verified
    via existence-check before filing this -- it checks whether "no movement/stalled"
    claims about GAPS are accurate (git log --grep), not whether the AC-coverage/
    outcome-verification engine correctly rejects bad submissions.
    
    Rough shape (not pre-sliced): a small, versioned fixture set of known-bad
    submissions (a stub that looks done but isn't, a test that asserts nothing
    meaningful, a diff that touches unrelated files, an outcome-verification target
    that's CI-green but doesn't perform its DoD) run against the live judgment organ
    on a schedule (nightly, alongside ChumpBench per docs/strategy/CHUMPBENCH.md SS6's
    regression-run pattern -- reuse that cadence, don't invent a new one). Alert if a
    known-bad fixture starts passing.
