- id: CREDIBLE-201
  domain: CREDIBLE
  title: "CREDIBLE: binary-age gauge stats the symlink not the target — freshness gate cries CRITICAL_STALE, scoreboard prints false build-date"
  status: done
  priority: P1
  effort: s
  description: |
    Two instruments report a ~95-day-old deployed binary while auto-deploy is verifiably working (target rebuilt 2026-08-05 17:48; PR #3478 merged 23:41Z same day). Root cause per evidence: binary-age is measured against ~/.local/bin/chump, a symlink created 2026-05-02, instead of resolving to ~/.cargo/bin/chump — 8251242s lands exactly on the symlink's date. Blast radius: (a) scripts/coord/freshness-preamble.sh (META-115) reports CRITICAL_STALE at every session start — a mandatory gate crying wolf trains agents to ignore it; (b) scripts/dev/mission-scoreboard.sh prints '(binary built 2026-05-02T11:47Z)' beside a passing (3) SHA check; (c) the scoreboard verdict hardcodes 'Next lever: MISSION-012 (self-deploy)' one line under 'MISSION-012 done'. Rough shape: stat -L (or readlink -f then stat) wherever binary mtime is read; derive the verdict's next-lever line from computed state instead of a literal; CI sibling with a symlink fixture so this class can't regress.
  acceptance_criteria:
    - freshness-preamble binary-age resolves symlinks (stat -L) and reports fresh when the deploy target is current
    - mission-scoreboard build-date resolves the target and matches the deployed SHA claim
    - verdict next-lever line is computed, not hardcoded — never names a goal the same run reports done
    - scripts/ci regression test covers the symlink case
  closed_date: '2026-08-06'
  closed_pr: 3482
  outcome_id: CREDIBLE-000
  evidence: |
    COMMAND: bash scripts/coord/freshness-preamble.sh; ls -la ~/.local/bin/chump ~/.cargo/bin/chump. OUTPUT: 'Freshness: CRITICAL_STALE (commits-behind=0, binary-age=8251242s, cron-health=unavailable, bootstrap=FAIL)' while ~/.cargo/bin/chump mtime is 2026-08-05 17:48 (rebuilt same day) and ~/.local/bin/chump is a symlink created 2026-05-02 05:47 pointing at it. THEORY: the gauge lstats the symlink instead of stat -L on the resolved target — 8251242s is ~95.5d which lands exactly on 2026-05-02; mission-scoreboard's '(binary built 2026-05-02T11:47Z)' shares the same artifact, and its verdict still prints 'Next lever: MISSION-012 (self-deploy)' one line under 'MISSION-012 done'. ALT: auto-deploy genuinely dead and the binary truly stale — refuted: target rebuilt today, scoreboard (3) SHA-vs-origin/main check passes (CREDIBLE-151), fleet shipping (PR #3478 merged 2026-08-05T23:41Z).

- id: CREDIBLE-202
  domain: CREDIBLE
  title: "CREDIBLE: almanac stale flag measures local checkout HEAD, not origin/main — weeks of behind-ness can read as fresh"
  status: done
  priority: P2
  effort: s
  description: |
    almanac_status reports stale:false when indexed_commit == the LOCAL checkout's HEAD — but the local checkout only moves when someone pulls. Observed 2026-08-05: Chump's checkout sat 15-16 commits behind origin/main; almanac reported indexed=true/stale=false the whole time, and the hourly refresh cron saw no HEAD move so it happily kept the old index. The gauge answers 'am I current with the checkout?' when consumers hear 'am I current with the repo?'. Same instrument class as Chump's symlink binary-age bug (CREDIBLE-201): the measurement is narrower than the question. Rough shape: (a) status gains behind_origin (git rev-list --count HEAD..origin/main after a cheap fetch, or last-fetch-age when offline); (b) stale semantics documented and split: stale_vs_checkout / behind_origin; (c) refresh cron optionally ff-pulls clean checkouts before deciding 'no HEAD move' (respect dirty checkouts — never touch them); (d) search grounding block surfaces behind_origin so a 0-hit or odd answer is inspectable. Fleet briefing already warns 'trust a 0-hit answer only after checking note/fallback_reason' — this extends that honesty to freshness.
  acceptance_criteria:
    - almanac_status exposes behind-origin distance or last-fetch age alongside stale
    - stale semantics documented in the tool description
    - refresh path cannot report fresh while origin/main is ahead and the checkout is clean
    - search grounding includes the new freshness signal
  notes: |
    Shipped in almanac repo directly (no chump PR — external-repo work): almanac commit 26975fc, 2026-08-06. status now reports origin {reference, behind, refs-vintage} from local refs (offline-safe) + loud origin_note when behind>0 or vintage unknown/stale. Verified live: chump checkout read 'behind 1' with note; almanac level+silent. 3 automated tests incl. real-clone behind-count e2e; DEPTH.md same commit.
  closed_date: '2026-08-06'
  skills_required: "external_repo:repairman29/almanac"
  outcome_id: CREDIBLE-000

