- id: CREDIBLE-217
  domain: CREDIBLE
  title: "CREDIBLE: [almanac] run the CONFIG organ fleet-wide on cadence — drift detection that fired once during UAT and never again"
  status: superseded
  priority: P2
  effort: m
  description: |
    The CONFIG organ already proved it finds real incoherence, once. During the comprehend UAT it surfaced CARGO_TARGET_DIR resolved 14 different ways across 171 sites in chump, three conflicting BEAST_MODE endpoint flags across 356 reads including a beast-mode.dev vs beastmode.dev typo-domain, OPENAI_API_KEY with 4 different defaults over 49 reads in Maclawd, and HEARTBEAT_DURATION set to both 2m and 8h. Every one of those is a live-config landmine. It ran as a one-off audit and has not run since. Make it a cadence job across all 103 registered repos, reporting only CHANGES in the drift set so the output stays signal — a first run establishes the baseline, subsequent runs report what is new or newly-resolved. Route material findings to holler so they become gaps through the existing bridge; this is genuinely a found-defect flow, which is what holler is for.
  acceptance_criteria:
    - a scheduled sweep runs the CONFIG organ across every registered repo and persists the drift set per repo
    - subsequent runs report DELTAS (new drift, resolved drift) not the full set — a report that repeats 171 known sites every run gets ignored, which is how the last one died
    - "per-ecosystem coverage honesty is preserved: a repo whose language has no CONFIG adapter reports None, never Full over nothing"
    - material findings route to holler with project set to the real repo slug so the existing holler-to-chump bridge files them (this IS a found-defect flow — the correct use of that intake)
    - benign sentinel variance (AGENT_ID placeholders, empty-string vs unset) is classified and suppressed by rule, not by hand, with the rule stated in the output
    - first sweep's summary recorded so the baseline is visible
  notes: |
    Superseded by EFFECTIVE-389 (code-posse) 2026-08-07. I filed this as a CONFIG-organ-only cadence sweep without checking the registry first — EFFECTIVE-389 already covered it and is strictly more general (all five organs, posse-pattern diffing, holler bridge conventions, placement decision). My two unique contributions (the stated-rule sentinel suppression, and the proven finding classes as a signal-quality bar) were folded into 389's AC list before closing this. This is exactly the DOC-082 dedupe failure that ZERO-WASTE-045 exists to prevent, committed by the agent who filed ZERO-WASTE-045 four hours earlier.
  skills_required: "external_repo:repairman29/almanac"

- id: CREDIBLE-218
  domain: CREDIBLE
  title: "CREDIBLE: gap-status reconciliation blind to non-open + pre-200-commit merges → 18 ghosts accumulated"
  status: done
  priority: P1
  effort: s
  acceptance_criteria:
    - "The change described by \"gap-status reconciliation blind to non-open + pre-200-commit merges → 18 ghosts accumulated\" is implemented in the relevant CREDIBLE code path(s)."
    - At least one test (cargo test or scripts/ci/test-*.sh) proves the new behavior and fails without the change.
    - cargo fmt + clippy --all-targets -D warnings + check pass; no regression to existing tests.
  closed_pr: 3506
  outcome_id: COTG
  evidence: |
    COMMAND: ship-queue reconciliation sweep of 18 stalled gaps (ready_to_ship/in_review/in_flight, 0 open PRs) 2026-08-07.
    OUTPUT: 10 of 18 were already merged on origin/main (verified SHAs e.g. INFRA-1811=31b11a22 #3318, META-094=7ce29ab7 #2503, INFRA-1032=5b5bfdda #1790) but status never reconciled. chump gap ship could NOT fix any: its UPDATE matches status='open' only (these were intermediate statuses) AND its merge-proof scans only git log main -n 200 (pre-July merges fall outside the window). Had to reconcile via chump gap set --status done --closed-pr N after independent SHA verification.
    THEORY: gap-status reconciliation has two structural blind spots — (a) only status='open' is reconcilable, so a gap that merges while ready_to_ship/in_review/in_flight is orphaned; (b) the 200-commit proof window silently fails for older merges. Together they guarantee ghost accumulation, which is the same status-provenance hole the hands-free merge loop (docs design) must not have — on merge, status must flip reliably regardless of prior status or merge age.
    ALT: widen chump gap ship to accept any non-terminal status + prove merge by gh/commit-grep over full history (not -n 200), OR drive reconciliation from the merge webhook (github_cache.db) so status flips at merge time and ghosts never form. Rejected leaving it manual — that is what produced 18 ghosts.

