- id: CREDIBLE-251
  domain: CREDIBLE
  title: the proof-of-merge test cannot say why it failed, and its gate is the last one on cargo test — 5 false reds today, one killed a ready PR
  status: done
  priority: P1
  effort: s
  acceptance_criteria:
    - "PRIMARY FIX — MAKE THE TEST ABLE TO EXPLAIN ITSELF. crates/chump-gap-store/src/lib.rs:5045-5089 runs 206 git subprocesses and discards EVERY exit status via 'let _ = Command...status()'. When anything fails in CI the only output is the assert message 'a merge >200 commits back must still be proven (CREDIBLE-218)'. That IS the 'no way to tell a flake from a real failure' problem, and it is in our code, not GitHub's. Capture .output() on each git call, assert success, and put git's stderr in the panic message. A test that cannot say why it failed must never be allowed to gate a merge"
    - "SECONDARY FIX — scripts/ci/test-status-flip-proof-of-merge.sh:32 is the LAST gate running 'cargo test' instead of nextest. The whole repo moved to nextest because of CREDIBLE-175's thread-shared env race (cargo test shares one process; --test-threads=1 does NOT isolate env). Two consequences: it carries a known nondeterminism class, and it sits OUTSIDE the INFRA-764 flake auto-rerun wrapper, which wraps nextest — so nothing ever retried it. Switch it to 'cargo nextest run -p chump-gap-store -E test(proof_of_merge)'"
    - "HONEST SCOPE, do not overclaim: the runner swap is NOT proven to be the cause. It could not be reproduced locally under either runner (3/3 green on CI's exact cargo test command). It is justified by consistency and by bringing the gate under the retry wrapper. The DIAGNOSTIC fix is what will actually identify the cause on the next occurrence — land it first and read the next failure"
    - "THE COMPOUNDING FAILURE IS THE REAL LESSON AND MUST BE FIXED TOO: a false-red gate fed an auto-closer that cannot distinguish a flake from a real failure, and it destroyed 24h of ready work. Either pr-failure-auto-rescue re-runs a failed required check once before closing, or a check outside the flake-rerun wrapper must not be allowed to trigger auto-close. Decide which, and write the reason down"
    - ALSO CLASSIFY IT in docs/process/KNOWN_FLAKES.yaml (INFRA-764) as an interim measure so the wrapper retries it while the root cause is found — but classification is NOT the fix and must not close this gap on its own
    - "VERIFY: land the diagnostics, then let CI run. The next occurrence must produce an actionable error naming the failing git invocation and its stderr. If 20 consecutive runs pass after the nextest switch, record that as evidence — not proof — and say so"
  closed_pr: 3556
  outcome_id: MISSION-010
  evidence: |
    COMMAND: gh run/job inspection across 2026-08-08 CI + local reruns | OUTPUT: credible218_merge_older_than_200_commits_is_proven failed in CI 5 times on 2026-08-08 (main 18:38, main 19:04, PR #3510 twice, PR #3537) and passes locally every time — cargo nextest 1/1 in 4.28s, and CI's exact 'cargo test -p chump-gap-store proof_of_merge -- --test-threads=1' 3/3 green locally. PR #3510's FINAL CI run was on the fully-fixed SHA 5573ebe6 with every real defect resolved, and this was its ONLY failure; pr-failure-auto-rescue (INFRA-3542) then closed it at 22:32 for 'stayed RED 23.2h' | THEORY: two compounding defects — (1) the test swallows every git exit status so it cannot report what actually went wrong, (2) its gate is the only one still on cargo test rather than nextest | ALT: rejected 'the test logic is wrong' — the CI log shows the gap-carrying commit landing correctly as '[main (root-commit) 13f86c2] EFFECTIVE-9999: the real merge, buried deep' followed by all 205 fillers, so the fixture built the history it intended

