    - "MECHANISM FOUND AND VERIFIED ON MAIN — no longer a hypothesis. scripts/ops/github-webhook-receiver.py: _extract_gap_ids (line 161) runs regex \\b([A-Z][A-Z-]+-\\d+)\\b over BOTH title AND body; _auto_flip_gaps_done (line 243, CREDIBLE-092) then runs `chump gap set <ID> --status done --closed-pr <N>` for EVERY id it found, on any merged PR. The receiver is RUNNING (1 process confirmed). That is the whole bug"
    - "IT EXPLAINS THE TWO THINGS THAT PREVIOUSLY DID NOT ADD UP: (1) it calls `gap set`, NOT `gap ship`, so INFRA-1392 PROOF-OF-MERGE never fires — that guard lives on the ship path only. Two routes to status=done, one guarded. (2) `gap set --status done` does not write closed_date, which is exactly why every falsely-closed gap has closed_pr set and closed_date empty"
    - "FULL DAMAGE, from the emitter own ambient trail: 30 gap_flipped_done_on_merge events across 8 PRs (#3551 flipped 7, #3544 5, #3556 5, #3554 3, #3549 3, #3553 3, #3548 2, #3550 2). Roughly 8 are legitimate (one per PR), so ~22 are collateral. It is hitting FLEET PRs, not just one session"
    - "THE SHARPEST ILLUSTRATION: PR #3556 changed exactly two files (docs/strategy/FACTORY_YIELD_2026-08-09.md and scripts/ops/first-pass-yield.sh) and closed FIVE gaps — CREDIBLE-273, CREDIBLE-175, DOC-096, CREDIBLE-251, RESILIENT-250. The document analysing why the factory loses work closed the two gaps it identified as the CAUSES of destroyed PRs, by citing them"
    - "CREDIBLE-092 INTENT WAS SOUND, do not simply revert it: auto-flip-on-merge.yml runs in CI where state.db does not exist, so merged gaps stayed open and got re-claimed (real ghost-gap waste). The receiver has filesystem access and fixes that. The EXTRACTION is what is wrong, not the idea"
    - "FIX 1 — key closure on INTENT, not prose: extract from the PR TITLE only, or require an explicit Closes: trailer. Never body text. Do NOT ask authors to stop cross-referencing; cross-references are how the registry stays navigable and are exactly what good ACs and handoff docs do"
