  status: blocked
  priority: P2
  effort: l
  acceptance_criteria:
    - "THE CLASS, stated so it can be hunted rather than stumbled upon: a component that is configured, installed, or asserted — and is not actually running, not actually wired, or not actually checking what its name claims. Its signature is SILENCE, not failure, which is why no failure-based metric can find it"
    - "WHY THIS IS P1 DESPITE NOTHING BEING BROKEN: the four found in one session include a linker that made every build slower than necessary and a notification channel whose death let PR #3510 be destroyed with nobody told. The cost is real and unbounded; only the detection is missing"
    - "BUILD THE SWEEP, and prefer cheap structural checks over cleverness. Candidate probes, each of which would have caught one of the four: (a) every launchd/plist job declared in scripts/launchd or ~/Library/LaunchAgents that has ZERO running processes; (b) every toml/config with enabled=true whose daemon is absent; (c) every CI gate whose grep target does not exist in the tree it greps — a check that matches nothing can never fail; (d) every apt/brew-installed tool that no script or env var references"
    - "START WITH (c), IT IS THE CHEAPEST AND HIGHEST YIELD: a gate asserting a path or symbol that no longer exists is a vacuous pass. CREDIBLE-237 found one by accident (test-stale-binary-ship-blocked.sh Test 3, a NEGATIVE assertion pointed at a file whose content had moved — so it could never fail again). Sweep scripts/ci for greps whose target is absent and report the count; that number is the size of the debt"
    - RUN IT ON A SCHEDULE, not once. A one-time sweep finds today instruments; the class regenerates every time code moves. Per ZERO-WASTE-036 an unscheduled instrument does not count as shipped — and the irony of an unscheduled rot-detector should not be lost on the implementer
    - REPORT AS FINDINGS, NOT FAILURES. These are not CI failures and must not block PRs; they are a queue of suspected-dead instruments for a human or a triage agent to confirm. False positives are expected — a gate can legitimately assert something absent
    - "VERIFY BY REPLAY: run the sweep against the tree as of 2026-08-08 and assert it independently finds operator-recall dead and the vacuous stale-binary assertion. A rot-detector that cannot rediscover known rot is itself rot"
  notes: |
