  status: done
  priority: P1
  effort: m
  acceptance_criteria:
    - "HOW THIS WAS FOUND, because the discovery path IS the argument: diagnosing CREDIBLE-268 required reverse-engineering the fleet own destructive behaviour from a raw log file. The truth sat in ambient.jsonl the whole time — 30 events, 8 PRs, unread. The artifact whose job is to describe that behaviour (EVENT_REGISTRY) was WRONG about it, and the consumers meant to watch it were phantom. An hour of forensics for something that should have been a query"
    - "DEFECT 1 — CONSUMERS ARE UNVERIFIED. Extend scripts/ci/test-event-registry-coverage.sh: for every kind with a consumers list, assert at least one named consumer actually references that kind in code. Today the gate greps for emitters only and never says the word consumer. Expect a large first-run backlog — report the COUNT of kinds whose declared consumers do not reference them, because that number is the real size of the write-only telemetry"
    - "DEFECT 2 — THE TRIGGER PROSE DRIFTED FROM THE CODE, IN THE EXACT WAY THAT HID THE BUG. The registry says the receiver flips gaps referenced in \"title/branch\". The code (_extract_gap_ids) reads title and BODY. That one-word difference IS CREDIBLE-268. Had the doc been true, the bug would have been visible on inspection. Add a drift check: the emitter named in the registry must exist, and where the trigger names fields, they should match what the emitter actually reads"
    - "WHY THIS IS P1 FOR AN AGENT OS: the whole model is emit signals, agents act on them. If any event may or may not be read and there is no way to tell which, then no claim about fleet behaviour is verifiable. This is the same defect class as CREDIBLE-237 (path-pinned gates), CREDIBLE-239 (env gate scanning only src/) and EFFECTIVE-407 (audit-ac blind to template ACs) — a contract that looks enforced and is not"
    - "DISTINCT FROM CREDIBLE-274, and both are needed: 274 covers instruments that STOPPED reporting (dead daemons, unwired tools). This covers instruments that report FAITHFULLY INTO A VOID while a contract claims someone is listening. Different failure, different detector"
    - WIRE AT LEAST ONE REAL CONSUMER for gap_flipped_done_on_merge as part of this — a destructive action (closing gaps) that nothing watches is how 30 collateral closures went unnoticed. The escalation channel shipped in RESILIENT-263 is the obvious sink for the destructive subset
    - "VERIFY: run the extended gate against main and assert it FAILS on gap_flipped_done_on_merge today. A consumer-check that passes on the known-broken case is worthless — that is the EFFECTIVE-407 lesson repeated"
  notes: |
