    (Aug 10, 182 LOC) is the anti-recurrence test: it shims `cargo`/
    `cargo-nextest` on PATH and asserts on the hook's ACTUAL captured argv
    (not a source grep), covering both the present and absent scenarios —
    reverting the runner-selection logic (even leaving the word "nextest"
    in a comment) fails it; (5) confirmed above; (6) bypass-trailer count:
    `git log --grep="Test-Gate-Bypass"` shows 275 commits before 2026-08-10
    vs. 7 since (out of 378 commits since), i.e. bypasses materially
