- id: EFFECTIVE-141
  domain: EFFECTIVE
  title: "EFFECTIVE: chump onboard provider cascade requests model 'gpt-5-mini' (404 on local API) — scout reaches provider but can't return proposals (BEAST-MODE 0->1)"
  status: done
  priority: P1
  effort: m
  description: |
    After EFFECTIVE-123 (clone-auth) + EFFECTIVE-133 (cascade runtime nesting)
    landed, `chump onboard https://github.com/repairman29/BEAST-MODE` clones and
    reaches the provider cascade with NO panic — but the cascade requests model
    'gpt-5-mini', which the local API 404s ("model 'gpt-5-mini' not found"). So
    the BEAST-MODE first-touch scout still can't return proposed gaps: the last
    link in the onboard 0->1 chain. The model appears hardcoded/misconfigured in
    crate::provider_cascade::build_provider (used by src/onboard.rs ~line 287).
  acceptance_criteria:
    - chump onboard's provider cascade requests a model the configured backend actually serves (no hardcoded 'gpt-5-mini' that 404s on the local API)
    - the cascade model is resolved from provider/cascade config with a sensible default that exists; an unavailable model yields a clear actionable error, not a silent empty result
    - "verified live: chump onboard https://github.com/repairman29/BEAST-MODE completes the full first-touch scan end-to-end and returns proposed gaps (the BEAST-MODE 0->1 scout acceptance case)"
    - a test covers the model-resolution path (default + override) without a live LLM call
  closed_pr: 3046
  outcome_id: MISSION-010

