- id: EFFECTIVE-220
  domain: EFFECTIVE
  title: "chump preflight: per-gate cargo output truncated at ~23k bytes — error line cut off, real diagnostic invisible (blocked 4 preflight retries today)"
  status: open
  priority: P2
  effort: xs
  description: |
    Modify the per‑gate cargo output capture logic in chump preflight (in `crates/chump-preflight/src/preflight.rs`) so that when a gate’s combined stdout/stderr exceeds ~23 k bytes, the user‑visible truncated output is guaranteed to contain the last 5 lines of the full output (preserving the critical error conclusion). Additionally, write the complete, untruncated output to a deterministic file path (`target/preflight-logs/<gate>.log`) and, on gate failure, print that path to stderr so the operator can inspect the full diagnostic.
    
    Target file(s):
    - crates/chump-preflight/src/preflight.rs
    - crates/chump-preflight/tests/preflight_truncation.rs
    
    (Spec enriched by chump-gap-enricher — EFFECTIVE-446. Original filer context preserved below.)
  acceptance_criteria:
    - "? Execute `chump preflight` on a crate that causes a gate’s cargo output to exceed 23 k bytes; confirm that the terminal output ends with the last 5 lines of the full output, including the line containing “error : could not compile”."
    - After the gate fails, verify that a file `target/preflight-logs/<gate>.log` exists and contains the complete, untruncated output of that gate’s cargo run.
    - Run `cargo test --test preflight_truncation` (a new test in `crates/chump-preflight/tests/preflight_truncation.rs`) that simulates a 30 k‑byte cargo error stream and asserts that the truncated output contains the last 5 lines and that the log file path is printed to stderr.
  notes: |
    Empirical evidence 2026-06-05: 4 preflight retries today (EFFECTIVE-216, RESILIENT-118) each showed truncated cargo output ending mid-"Checking" line, no error visible. Had to re-run cargo clippy --workspace directly to see the actual diagnostic (turned out clippy was fine; failures were sccache/reaper races). Truncation made root-cause diagnosis 10× slower than necessary.
  opened_date: '2026-07-26'
  outcome_id: EFFECTIVE-000

- id: EFFECTIVE-221
  domain: EFFECTIVE
  title: "EFFECTIVE: chump-commit auto-inject Net-new-docs trailer + surface commit-msg-hook rejections"
  status: blocked
  priority: P2
  effort: s
  description: |
    Adding a new docs/*.md file requires a 'Net-new-docs: +N' commit trailer (CHUMP_DOCS_DELTA_CHECK), enforced at the commit-msg stage. chump-commit.sh PRINTS the requirement during pre-commit but does NOT auto-inject the trailer, so the commit-msg hook rejects the commit — and when chump-commit output is piped (e.g. '| tail'), the pipe's exit code masks the rejection (cost 2 failed commit attempts on CREDIBLE-105 before manual git-log verification caught it). chump-commit already computes the docs delta (it prints 'net +1'), so it can either auto-append the trailer or fail loudly.
  acceptance_criteria:
    - "chump-commit.sh auto-injects the correct 'Net-new-docs: +N' trailer when the staged set adds N net-new docs/*.md files (matching the commit-msg gate), OR"
    - "if not auto-injecting, chump-commit.sh exits NON-ZERO and prints a clear 'COMMIT REJECTED — add Net-new-docs: +N trailer' as its LAST output line (survives a '"
    - " tail' pipe)"
