- id: EFFECTIVE-342
  domain: EFFECTIVE
  title: agent-run implement produces correct code but never persists it (uses read-only tools only) — blocks zero-touch CREATE
  status: done
  priority: P2
  effort: m
  description: |
    Surfaced by the first live EFFECTIVE-341 --implement lap. THE blocker to zero-touch CREATE (vision → working tool).
    
    WHAT HAPPENED: chump bench run --implement drove chump agent-run with the vision. The agent AUTHORED a correct rename_photos.py IN ITS REPLY TEXT (EXIF DateTimeOriginal → strptime → os.rename, argparse CLI) but executed ONLY read-only tools (list_dir, read_file) — never write_file. File exists nowhere; agent-run exited 0; acceptance failed.
    
    ROOT CAUSE (diagnosed):
    - write_file IS registered — build_chump_agent_cli (agent_factory.rs:52) uses register_from_inventory = FULL toolset incl write_file (tool_inventory.rs:101). Tool available; model didn't call it.
    - agent-run runs on provider_cascade::global_provider() = the FREE cloud cascade (Groq/Cerebras/Mistral/OpenRouter/Gemini/…), NOT Anthropic. Exactly the models tool_inventory.rs:131-138 flags as prone to 'spend their whole iteration budget on blind list_dir/read_file and never reach patch_file' (EFFECTIVE-005). Author-in-reply-then-stop is that failure class.
    
    So code-AUTHORING works on a free model; reliable code-PERSISTING does not.
    
    FIX DIRECTIONS:
    (a) Route CREATE-implement agent-run to a capable provider (Anthropic via ANTHROPIC_API_KEY/OAUTH) not the free cost-cascade — needs a provider-selection knob on agent-run.
    (b) Bump CHUMP_AGENT_MAX_ITER (default 25) + system-prompt nudge that the deliverable is files-on-disk.
    (c) Re-run create-photo-renamer --implement to CONFIRM write_file fires + file lands.
    
    ACCEPTANCE: a --implement lap leaves the authored file on disk in the scored clone dir. Pillar: EFFECTIVE.
  acceptance_criteria:
    - "The change described by \"agent-run implement produces correct code but never persists it (uses read-only tools only) — blocks zero-touch CREATE\" is implemented in the relevant EFFECTIVE code path(s)."
    - At least one test (cargo test or scripts/ci/test-*.sh) proves the new behavior and fails without the change.
    - cargo fmt + clippy --all-targets -D warnings + check pass; no regression to existing tests.
  closed_date: '2026-07-31'
