    - "TOOL-CAPABILITY IS QUERYABLE AND DIRECTLY FIXES THE MEASURED FAILURE: supported_parameters contains 'tools'. Measured 2026-08-07: 17 free-priced models, 14 tool-capable. EFFECTIVE-366 escalates to Claude because 'the free/sub models all avoid str_replace' — but slot selection today never checks whether a model advertises tool support at all. Filter on it before blaming the model"
    - "CAPABILITY-CLASS ROUTING, the thing Jeff actually asked for: rank slots per TASK CLASS, not one global order. Chump already carries the taxonomy (work / cursor_improve / doc_hygiene / battle_qa / research / opportunity / discovery) and the routing machinery (CascadeStrategy::TaskAware and provider_bandit Thompson Sampling) — both built, both OFF by default (strategy falls back to Priority). Wire the tender's rankings into them rather than adding a third mechanism"
    - "RANK ON MEASURED FITNESS, NOT ADVERTISED SPECS: provider_quality.rs already records success/failure/latency and TOOL-CALL success per slot and drives demotion. Join that observed record to the indexed metadata. A model that advertises tools but fails tool-calls in practice must rank below one that succeeds — advertised capability is a claim, tool_call_result is an outcome"
    - "VERIFY LIMITS, REPORT DRIFT, NEVER AUTO-EDIT .env — folds in CREDIBLE-227: probe rate-limit headers and /v1/models per configured slot, compare against declared RPM/RPD/CONTEXT_K, and file disagreement as a finding. Receipt for why: slots 4 and 8 both declare model=gemini-2.5-flash yet differ 57x on RPD (86400 vs 1500), and slots 12-15 declare no limits at all"
    - "DEPRECATION + CONNECTIVITY WATCH: expiration_date and model presence in /v1/models catch a configured model that has been retired; a dead key or moved base URL surfaces the same way. Today a retired model fails silently at call time, mid-task"
    - "BIG-CONTEXT ROUTING IS FREE MONEY LEFT ON THE TABLE: free tool-capable models exist at 1,000,000 context (nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b:free) and several at 262,144. Nothing today routes 'this task needs a huge window' to them — the cascade orders by priority and rate limit only"
    - "OUTPUT IS A RANKED, DATED ARTIFACT the fleet and a human can both read, refreshed on a schedule (launchd per SCHEDULING_LAYERS.md — it must survive session close). Not a one-shot script someone remembers to run: see ZERO-WASTE-036, this fleet's most repeated failure is the built-and-never-scheduled instrument"
