- id: EFFECTIVE-441
  domain: EFFECTIVE
  title: "ATC re-attempt loop: an unverified_ship gap is re-picked forever, burning inference (Jeff-flagged). The worker cooldown (worker.sh ~L616/L890) ONLY fires on pre-pick preflight FAIL (claimed/done/missing); a gap that is claimed, worked, and returns rc=0 unverified_ship (agent ran but produced no merging PR) is released straight back to open and re-picked next cycle indefinitely. Attempts are not tracked in the gap store (no cooldown/attempt/fail column) — only in cooldown files keyed on preflight-fail. LIVE PROOF: RESILIENT-354 re-picked by agent-2 at cycle 130 AND 135 (5 cycles apart) with no ship. This wastes inference AND hides genuinely-stuck gaps (the fleet cannot tell 'hard gap it cannot crack' from 'not tried yet'). FIX IN THE OS (ATC/dispatch): persist a per-gap unverified_ship attempt counter; after N consecutive unverified_ships (e.g. 3) COOL DOWN the gap (backoff window, not immediately re-pickable) AND escalate — bump model tier (sonnet->opus) OR route to decompose-on-review (gap may be too big) OR after M total park it as needs-human/needs-decompose. AC: seed a gap the agent cannot ship; after N unverified_ships it is NOT immediately re-picked (cooldown observable), the model/route escalates, and after M it parks with a reason; prove no single gap is re-attempted >M times in a row; RESILIENT-354-class loop cannot recur. Pairs with the escalation ladder (free->sub->sonnet->opus, that is intra-attempt; this is the cross-cycle loop) + the AC/decompose organ."
