- id: INFRA-1014
  domain: INFRA
  title: "CREDIBLE: PWA auth layer (CHUMP_WEB_TOKEN config + enforcement)"
  status: done
  priority: P1
  effort: s
  description: |
    Today the PWA assumes localhost-only access. CHUMP_WEB_TOKEN env var exists in PWA_STARTUP.md but has no UI to configure and (verify during implementation) inconsistent enforcement. For the demo, especially if recording over a tunneled URL or showing on a non-laptop, we need: (a) clear UI to set the token via /settings (post-INFRA-988/989), (b) middleware that enforces Bearer-token on all /api/* routes when CHUMP_WEB_TOKEN is set, (c) localhost-bypass kept as default to avoid breaking dev flow, (d) prominent UI warning on /settings if CHUMP_WEB_TOKEN is unset AND bind address is not localhost (e.g. 0.0.0.0). Rough shape: (a) settings UI field with mask + Replace pattern (reuse INFRA-989's secret components), (b) src/web_server.rs middleware that checks Authorization: Bearer header against env CHUMP_WEB_TOKEN, (c) login page when token is set but missing/wrong — single input field, validates against /api/auth/check, stores token in localStorage with expiry, (d) on unbind from localhost (CHUMP_WEB_BIND or similar), warn loudly until token set.
  acceptance_criteria:
    - Settings UI exposes CHUMP_WEB_TOKEN field with secret-input pattern (presence-only GET, test-before-store POST)
    - "When CHUMP_WEB_TOKEN env var set, middleware in src/web_server.rs requires Authorization: Bearer <token> on /api/* (except /api/health)"
    - "Localhost bypass: requests from 127.0.0.1/[::1] skip the check by default (CHUMP_WEB_REQUIRE_TOKEN=1 to disable bypass)"
    - "Missing/bad token returns 401 with WWW-Authenticate: Bearer realm header"
    - Login page in web/v2/ accepts token, validates via POST /api/auth/check, stores in localStorage
    - Settings page shows warning banner if CHUMP_WEB_TOKEN unset AND server bound to non-localhost address
    - "Test: bind to 0.0.0.0 without token → warning visible; bind with token + bad Authorization → 401; with correct token → routes accessible"
  closed_date: '2026-05-14'
  outcome_id: MISSION-010

- id: INFRA-1015
  domain: INFRA
  title: "EFFECTIVE: chump init flow from PWA (fresh-repo onboarding)"
  status: done
  priority: P1
  effort: s
  description: |
    Demo scene 5: when the operator picks a repo path that lacks .chump/state.db, the PWA should offer to initialize it — not error out. chump init exists as a CLI command. We need a web-facing equivalent. Rough shape: (a) the first-run wizard (INFRA-990) detects 'no state.db' and offers 'Initialize Chump in this repo' as a sub-step, (b) new POST /api/repo/init endpoint that wraps chump init subprocess call (creates .chump/, state.db, default gap registry mirror, installs hooks via scripts/setup/install-hooks.sh), (c) post-init, optionally seed 1-3 starter gaps (e.g. 'add a /health endpoint to this server') from a built-in template list — provides immediate work for the demo, (d) safety: refuse to init if the path is outside operator-blessed dirs (default: home dir tree) unless CHUMP_INIT_ANYWHERE=1, (e) confirmation dialog before running — 'This will create .chump/ and install pre-commit hooks. Continue?'
  acceptance_criteria:
    - POST /api/repo/init {path} validates path is within allowed parent dirs, runs chump init in that path, returns success/failure with stderr on failure
    - Wizard (INFRA-990) detects missing state.db and surfaces 'Initialize this repo' step with confirmation dialog
    - Post-init, optional checkbox 'Seed 3 starter gaps' adds template gaps to the registry
    - Hooks installed via scripts/setup/install-hooks.sh after init
    - "Refuses paths outside CHUMP_INIT_ALLOWED_ROOTS (default: /Users/jeffadkins tree); CHUMP_INIT_ANYWHERE=1 bypasses"
    - "Test: point at empty /tmp/test-repo, verify /api/repo/init creates state.db + hooks; verify second call is idempotent (succeeds without overwriting)"
  closed_date: '2026-05-15'
  closed_pr: 1936
  outcome_id: MISSION-010

- id: INFRA-1016
  domain: INFRA
  title: "RESILIENT: pr-rescue --rest-only mode (survives GraphQL exhaustion)"
  status: done
  priority: P1
  effort: xs
  description: |
    Today every rescue tool (pr-rescue, queue-driver, bot-merge) uses gh pr * GraphQL shortcuts.
    When GraphQL bucket hits 0/5000 (1-2x per active day), all rescue is gagged for ~30 min.
    REST core bucket stays healthy in parallel (4868/5000 typical). Adding a --rest-only mode
    to pr-rescue.sh as the minimum-viable rescue path lets the operator still recover stuck PRs
    during GraphQL exhaustion. REST merge is immediate (no auto-merge); accepted limitation:
    only use when PR is already green and you want to force-land it now.
  closed_pr: 1685
  outcome_id: MISSION-010

