- id: INFRA-1360
  domain: INFRA
  title: "ZERO-WASTE: chump-gh-app crate — JWT installation-token generation for INFRA-1076 lane isolation"
  status: done
  priority: P1
  effort: m
  acceptance_criteria:
    - "New Rust crate at `crates/chump-gh-app/` with Cargo.toml + src/lib.rs. Dependencies: jsonwebtoken = \"9\", reqwest = { version = \"0.12\", features = [\"json\", \"rustls-tls\"] }, serde = { features = [\"derive\"] }, serde_json, chrono, anyhow."
    - "Public API:"
    - "  pub struct AppCredentials { app_id: u64, private_key_pem: String, installation_id: u64 }"
    - "  pub struct InstallationToken { token: String, expires_at: chrono::DateTime<Utc> }"
    - "  pub async fn generate_jwt(app_id: u64, private_key_pem: &str) -> Result<String> — RS256-signed JWT with iss=app_id, exp=now+10min (max GitHub allows is 10min)."
    - "  pub async fn fetch_installation_token(creds: &AppCredentials) -> Result<InstallationToken> — POST /app/installations/{id}/access_tokens with the JWT as Bearer; parses response { token, expires_at }."
    - "  pub fn load_apps_config(path: &Path) -> Result<HashMap<Lane, AppCredentials>> — reads ~/.chump/github_apps.toml: keys = `critical`, `background`; each entry has `app_id`, `private_key_path`, `installation_id`. Returns a map; missing lanes are simply absent (no error)."
    - "Token-file output format (the bash side reads this):"
    - "  ~/.chump/oauth-token-<lane>.json with {\"token\": \"ghs_...\", \"written_at\": \"...\", \"expires_at\": \"...\"} — matches the existing oauth-token.json shape from src/auth.rs."
    - "Unit tests (≥5) in tests/ or src/lib.rs:"
    - "  - generate_jwt produces a 3-part JWT with iss=app_id (decode without verify, check the claim)"
    - "  - load_apps_config with both lanes present returns 2-entry map"
    - "  - load_apps_config with only critical lane returns 1-entry map (background lane silently absent)"
    - "  - load_apps_config with malformed TOML returns Err with clear message"
    - "  - InstallationToken.expires_at parses RFC3339 correctly"
    - No live GitHub calls in unit tests (the JWT generation + TOML parsing + struct construction are all pure-function or local-file).
    - "Integration test (gated on env CHUMP_GH_APP_INTEGRATION=1): if real App credentials are configured, exercises the full fetch_installation_token round-trip against api.github.com. Default skip preserves CI signal without coupling to real Apps."
    - "Out of scope: bash-side token consumption (already shipped in INFRA-1076 PR #2095), rotator cron (INFRA-1361), runbook (INFRA-1362)."
  closed_date: '2026-05-15'
  outcome_id: MISSION-010

- id: INFRA-1361
  domain: INFRA
  title: "ZERO-WASTE: chump gh-token rotate cron — refresh per-lane installation tokens every 50min (INFRA-1076 follow-up)"
  status: done
  priority: P1
  effort: s
  acceptance_criteria:
    - "Add `chump gh-token rotate` subcommand to src/main.rs (or src/gh_token.rs as new module). Reads ~/.chump/github_apps.toml via chump_gh_app::load_apps_config (INFRA-1360). For each configured lane, calls chump_gh_app::fetch_installation_token, writes the result to ~/.chump/oauth-token-<lane>.json with chmod 600."
    - "Behaviour:"
    - "  - When ~/.chump/github_apps.toml is absent → exit 0 silently (operator hasnt set up Apps yet). Emits kind=gh_token_rotate_noop with reason=apps_config_missing once per invocation."
    - "  - When TOML is malformed → exit 2 with stderr message pointing at the path + parse error."
    - "  - When a specific lane fetch fails (network, JWT rejection, etc.) → log to stderr, continue to next lane, exit 1 at end if any lane failed. The other lanes still get fresh tokens."
    - "  - On success per lane: emit kind=gh_token_rotated with {ts, lane, expires_at}."
    - launchd plist at scripts/setup/launchd/com.chump.gh-token-rotate.plist for macOS install — runs `chump gh-token rotate` every 50 min (10-min slack on the 60-min token expiry). scripts/setup/install-gh-token-rotate-launchd.sh installs the plist into ~/Library/LaunchAgents. Linux operators use cron with the same cadence (documented in INFRA-1362 runbook).
    - "CI test scripts/ci/test-gh-token-rotate-noop.sh: runs `chump gh-token rotate` in a HOME with no github_apps.toml, asserts exit 0 + gh_token_rotate_noop emit. No live GitHub calls."
    - "Documentation: docs/observability/EVENT_REGISTRY.yaml gets two new kinds (gh_token_rotate_noop, gh_token_rotated) per INFRA-754."
    - "Out of scope: actual GitHub Apps creation (operator action — INFRA-1362 runbook), the chump-gh-app crate itself (INFRA-1360)."
  closed_pr: 2123
  outcome_id: MISSION-010

- id: INFRA-1362
  domain: INFRA
  title: "EFFECTIVE: OPERATOR_RUNBOOK.md — one-shot setup checklist for INFRA-1076 GitHub App installations"
  status: done
  priority: P1
  effort: xs
  acceptance_criteria:
    - "New file docs/process/OPERATOR_RUNBOOK.md with a top-level table-of-contents and a dedicated section \"INFRA-1076: split GitHub App lane installations (one-shot setup)\" containing:"
    - "  1. Why: the multi-hour secondary-mutation gag on the operator user account (live evidence from 2026-05-14 session) blocks ship-blocking merges when a sweep saturates the per-user limit. Lane-isolated App installations give critical + background flows their own quota counters."
    - "  2. Prerequisite: GitHub admin access to the org and the repo (repairman29/chump)."
    - "  3. Step 1: Create the chump-critical GitHub App in github.com/settings/apps. Scopes: repo: contents (write), pull-requests (write), statuses (write), checks (write), metadata (read). Generate + download the private-key .pem file."
    - "  4. Step 2: Same as Step 1 but for chump-background. Same scopes."
    - "  5. Step 3: Install both Apps on the repository in github.com/settings/installations."
    - "  6. Step 4: Create ~/.chump/github_apps.toml chmod 600 with the structure:"
    - "       [critical]"
    - "       app_id = <Id from app settings>"
    - "       private_key_path = \"/Users/<you>/.chump/keys/chump-critical.pem\""
    - "       installation_id = <Installation Id from /api/installations>"
    - "       [background]"
    - "       (same fields)"
    - "  7. Step 5: Install the rotator cron — on macOS run `bash scripts/setup/install-gh-token-rotate-launchd.sh`; on Linux add `*/50 * * * * <repo>/target/release/chump gh-token rotate` to crontab."
    - "  8. Step 6: Verify with `chump gh-token rotate` (one-shot manual run); inspect ~/.chump/oauth-token-{critical,background}.json files exist with chmod 600."
    - "  9. Step 7: Verify lane routing in flight — run `CHUMP_GH_CALL_CRITICALITY=background chump_gh api rate_limit` and confirm via `gh api rate_limit` (without the env) that the two return DIFFERENT rate_limit.remaining values (separate quota buckets)."
    - "  10. Recovery: when chump-gh-app crate (INFRA-1360) is updated and the App installations are revoked or rotated, re-run Steps 1–6 to refresh credentials."
    - "Cross-references: link from INFRA-1076 PR body + AC to this runbook section once the runbook lands. Link from docs/process/CLAUDE_GOTCHAS.md secondary-mutation section to this runbook as the structural fix."
    - "Out of scope: command-line tool that AUTOMATES the App creation (still requires browser GitHub Settings UI per GitHub policy)."
  closed_date: '2026-05-15'
  closed_pr: 2099
  outcome_id: MISSION-010

