    - "Out of scope: refactoring pre-commit-rust-first.sh to read from -m directly via git stash/temp file (more invasive)"
  closed_date: '2026-05-15'
  closed_pr: 2118
  outcome_id: MISSION-010

- id: INFRA-1368
  domain: INFRA
  title: "ZERO-WASTE: materialize mergeStateStatus column in .chump/github_cache.db pr_state — webhook receiver writes from pull_request payload, gh-shim/pr-view-translate.py serves it from cache (kills the dominant cache_miss source on every fleet poll)"
  status: done
  priority: P1
  effort: s
  description: |
    Investigated 2026-05-15: smee.io webhook tunnel + receiver are healthy and 71 PRs are cached fresh-seconds, but last-1000-ambient shows 3 cache_miss / 1 cache_hit with ALL misses being mergeStateStatus lookups. The dominant fleet query (BLOCKED scan in bot-merge, queue-driver, pr-rescue) takes a cache miss every time and falls back to direct gh REST — defeating most of the smee architecture. Pure infra-on-disk that the pipeline already exists for; just a missing column + write path + read path. Small surface (one column, three Python edits). Pairs with broader INFRA-1318 (Liaison Phase 2) but is the 80% win without the deps.
  acceptance_criteria:
    - Add merge_state_status TEXT column to pr_state in .chump/github_cache.db (nullable; schema migration in scripts/ops/github-webhook-receiver.py via ALTER TABLE IF NOT EXISTS pattern)
    - github-webhook-receiver.py on pull_request webhook event writes mergeStateStatus from payload (BLOCKED
    - CLEAN
    - DIRTY
    - UNKNOWN
    - UNSTABLE
    - BEHIND
    - DRAFT) into the new column
    - scripts/coord/lib/gh-shim/pr-view-translate.py recognizes mergeStateStatus in the requested fields and serves from cache when present, falls back to live gh only when null (cold start before first webhook)
    - scripts/ops/github-cache-reconcile.sh backfill pass populates the column for existing rows using one GraphQL call per PR (background-criticality, throttled)
    - "CI test scripts/ci/test-cache-mergestatestatus.sh: stub webhook delivery; assert column written; gh-shim invocation serves from cache (cache_hit emit)"
    - "Telemetry: existing cache_hit/cache_miss kinds already cover this; the shipping signal is the fleet-wide cache_miss rate drop visible in last-hour ambient histogram"
  closed_date: '2026-05-15'
  closed_pr: 2105
  outcome_id: MISSION-010

- id: INFRA-1369
  domain: INFRA
  title: "EFFECTIVE: cut chump v0.1.2 release — brew tap pins 2026-04-30 v0.1.1 binary that predates --version handler (INFRA-148, merged 2026-05-02), causing every FTUE CI run to fail because v0.1.1 falls through to Ollama agent loop on `chump --version`"
  status: done
  priority: P1
  effort: xs
  acceptance_criteria:
    - "Root cause: brew tap repairman29/homebrew-chump pins prebuilt v0.1.1 (released 2026-04-30). The --version handler in src/main.rs:666-674 was added 2026-05-02 in PR #767 (INFRA-148, commit d5242719). The released binary lacks it, so 'chump --version' falls through to the LLM agent loop and tries Ollama at OPENAI_API_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1, exit 1. Verified via gh run view 25943055744."
    - Cut release v0.1.2 from current main HEAD via the canonical release workflow; confirm the four target-triple binaries (aarch64-apple-darwin, x86_64-apple-darwin, aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu, x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu) publish as chump-<triple>.tar.xz with sha256 sums.
    - "Update repairman29/homebrew-chump tap formula to v0.1.2 with new sha256 sums. Note: the Formula/chump.rb in THIS repo is dead/stale (points at main.tar.gz, not what brew tap installs). Verify on a clean macos-15 runner that 'brew install chump && chump --version' exits 0."
    - ftue-clean-machine-2026.yml passes end-to-end on a PR that touches scripts/dispatch/** (currently fails on every such PR since 2026-05-02).
    - This repo's stale Formula/chump.rb either deleted OR replaced with a clear comment that the canonical formula lives at github.com/repairman29/homebrew-chump (today's investigation lost 30 minutes to this misleading file).
    - File follow-up gap for a release-staleness gate that fails CI when the latest GitHub release is > 14 days behind main HEAD, so this drift is caught structurally.
    - "Test: re-run 'gh workflow run ftue-clean-machine-2026.yml --ref <pr-branch>' on an open PR; assert the chump --version step prints a version and exits 0."
  closed_date: '2026-05-15'
  closed_pr: 2114
  outcome_id: MISSION-010

- id: INFRA-1370
  domain: INFRA
  title: "CREDIBLE: chump audit aha-sweep — walks code/runtime/effect triangle for every feature shipped last 30d, emits kind=audit_finding when any leg diverges (replaces ad-hoc operator triangulation that found INFRA-1368)"
  status: done
  priority: P1
  effort: m
  description: |
    The smee-mergeStateStatus discovery on 2026-05-15 (filed as INFRA-1368) came from operator triangulating: (1) code presence via grep, (2) runtime state via launchctl/cache schema, (3) measured effect via ambient cache_hit count. CI/SLO dashboards check legs 1+2 but almost never 3, so 'mission failure under green uptime' ships undetected. This gap systematizes the triangulation as a recurring sweep — turns 'aha moments dependent on operator curiosity' into 'guaranteed detection within hourly cycle'. Pairs with INFRA-1371 (per-kind effect_metric declaration).
  acceptance_criteria:
    - "New CLI subcommand: chump audit aha-sweep [--window-days 30] [--json] walks the code/runtime/effect triangle for each candidate feature"
    - "Candidate sources: (a) src/ pub fn defined in last N days (git log -p --since), (b) /api/* routes registered in src/web_server.rs, (c) kinds registered in docs/observability/EVENT_REGISTRY.yaml, (d) PWA web components defined in web/v2/app.js"
    - "For each candidate, check 3 legs: PLUMBING (code/tests/docs present), HEARTBEAT (runtime evidence: launchd entry / cron / route serving / component mounted), EFFECT (measurable output: emit count, call count, request count, render count last N days)"
    - "Emit one kind=audit_finding to ambient.jsonl per divergence with body {ts, kind, feature_id, feature_class, plumbing_ok, heartbeat_ok, effect_ok, effect_metric_name, effect_observed, effect_expected, severity (\"warn\""
    - "\"alert\")}"
    - Register kind=audit_finding in EVENT_REGISTRY.yaml
    - Exit non-zero when any feature has plumbing_ok=true heartbeat_ok=true effect_ok=false (i.e. the smee case)
    - CI test scripts/ci/test-audit-aha-sweep.sh seeds a synthetic feature in each leg-divergence quadrant, asserts the sweep finds and emits
    - docs/process/AUDIT_FRAMEWORK.md documents the triangle model + how to add a new feature class
    - Scheduled launchd job runs hourly, surfaces findings in PWA <chump-view-audit-findings> panel
  closed_pr: 2122
  outcome_id: MISSION-010

