  status: done
  priority: P1
  effort: s
  description: |
    Verified 2026-05-17 03:20 UTC: (1) sentinel mechanism works — worker.sh:295-299 checks .chump/fleet-paused before claim cycle, CHUMP_IGNORE_WASTE_PAUSE=1 bypass exists; (2) sentinel is currently only set by scripts/coord/waste-spike-detector.sh on waste-% threshold; (3) chump health --slo-check correctly exits 1 on breach (verified directly with /opt/homebrew/bin/chump → RC=1 on the 2 active breaches: L1-SLO-1 silent_agent + L2-SLO-2 waste 58%); (4) MISSION_YIELD.md Floor rule states "≥10 yield, below which pause and investigate before claiming new work" — doctrine, not enforced; (5) docs/process/FLEET_SLOS.md breach response ladder — defined but only acts via worker.sh waste-spike path. WHAT IS MISSING: a daemon that runs chump health --slo-check + pipeline-jam check (% BLOCKED PRs over rolling window) and sets/clears .chump/fleet-paused based on results, AND a chump gap reserve admission gate that respects the sentinel. Live evidence of need: 10/10 open PRs BLOCKED right now (100% jam), waste at 58% (11x target), workers still claiming new work — exactly the cascade the lid would prevent. INFRA-1522 covers the related chump fleet up startup gate but not gap-reserve admission.
