- id: INFRA-1645
  domain: INFRA
  title: "RESILIENT: paramedic daemon broken (LLM-model 404) — re-do of INFRA-1597"
  status: done
  priority: P2
  effort: s
  description: |
    Modify the `daemon` function in `crates/chump-paramedic/src/paramedic.rs` to handle LLM model 404 errors gracefully by classifying them as transient failures, applying exponential backoff with jitter (mirroring the `organ_watchdog_in_backoff` logic from `scripts/ops/organ-watchdog.sh`), emitting structured events (`model_unavailable`, `paramedic_healthy`, `permanent_failure`, `cost_report`), and adding a `--smoke-test` flag that performs a quick observability check; also create `crates/chump-paramedic/tests/resilience.rs` with an integration test that validates the resilience behavior against a mock LLM endpoint.
    
    Target file(s):
    - crates/chump-paramedic/src/paramedic.rs
    - crates/chump-paramedic/tests/resilience.rs
    
    (Spec enriched by chump-gap-enricher — EFFECTIVE-446. Original filer context preserved below.)
  acceptance_criteria:
    - The `daemon` function in `crates/chump-paramedic/src/paramedic.rs` classifies HTTP 404 responses as transient failures, retries with exponential backoff (configurable via env vars `PARAMEDIC_BACKOFF_BASE_MS`, `PARAMEDIC_BACKOFF_MAX_MS`, `PARAMEDIC_BACKOFF_JITTER`), and emits a `model_unavailable` event on each retry; any other 4xx (except 429) is treated as permanent and emits a `permanent_failure` event before exiting.
    - Running `cargo test --test resilience` passes, where the test `simulate_404_and_recovery` in `crates/chump-paramedic/tests/resilience.rs` starts the daemon against a mock server returning 404, then 200, and asserts that the daemon log contains `model_unavailable` followed by `paramedic_healthy` within 30 seconds.
    - "Executing `cargo run --bin paramedic -- --smoke-test` exits 0 and prints a JSON line with `event: cost_report` containing numeric fields `tokens_used` and `estimated_cost_usd` after a successful dummy LLM call."
    - The `organ_watchdog_in_backoff` function in `scripts/ops/organ-watchdog.sh` is not modified, but the paramedic daemon's backoff algorithm is documented in a comment referencing that function for consistency.
  notes: |
    [2026-08-28T09:20:05Z] CREDIBLE-178: closed via PR #4290 with UNCOVERED acceptance criteria "misses":[2,3]. Verify the work is complete before trusting status=done.
  opened_date: '2026-07-26'
  closed_date: '2026-08-28'
  closed_pr: 4290
  outcome_id: MISSION-010

- id: INFRA-1646
  domain: INFRA
  title: "RESILIENT: block chump claim when active lease already exists (re-do of INFRA-1412)"
  status: done
  priority: P2
  effort: s
  description: |
    In `run_claim`, add a guard at the top that calls `is_session_lease_alive` for the current session; if an active lease already exists, skip the claim attempt, emit a `ClaimBlocked` event, and return immediately without touching the lease store.
    
    Target file(s):
    - crates/chump-atomic-claim/src/atomic_claim.rs
    
    (Spec enriched by chump-gap-enricher — EFFECTIVE-446. Original filer context preserved below.)
  acceptance_criteria:
    - In crates/chump-atomic-claim/src/atomic_claim.rs, calling `run_claim` with a `ClaimArgs` whose session already has an active lease (per `is_session_lease_alive`) returns early without writing to the lease store.
    - When the guard blocks a claim, a `ClaimBlocked` event is emitted containing the session ID and the existing lease ID.
    - A unit test in the same file exercises the blocked path by pre-seeding an active lease, then calling `run_claim`, and asserts no new lease is created and the `ClaimBlocked` event is observable.
    - Running `cargo test -p chump-atomic-claim` passes all existing tests plus the new blocked-claim test.
  notes: |
    [2026-08-27T13:47:06Z] CREDIBLE-178: closed via PR #4273 with UNCOVERED acceptance criteria "misses":[0,1,2,3]. Verify the work is complete before trusting status=done.
