- id: INFRA-1727
  domain: INFRA
  title: "CREDIBLE: docs/HIDDEN_GEMS.md spec + auto-populate from chump skill list + content-bot findings (surface under-discovered primitives)"
  status: done
  priority: P1
  effort: s
  description: |
    Phase 3 Evangelism gap from the multi-agent-factory ingestion-engine review (2026-05-22). New users miss valuable primitives (chump-coord watch, chump gap consolidate, chump revert, PWA, the skills layer) because there is no curated showcase doc. The Evangelist content bot (META-066) will draft material for this surface once running, but no SPEC exists for what gets surfaced or how the doc is structured. Rough shape: (a) docs/HIDDEN_GEMS.md as the user-facing surface with structured sections (CLI commands, agent tools, config knobs, hidden features); (b) scripts/dev/build-hidden-gems.sh auto-populates skeleton from chump skill list + scripts/README.md catalog + chump-mcp.json + ambient EVENT_REGISTRY.yaml; (c) docs/HIDDEN_GEMS_CURATED.yaml operator overlay for hand-picked entries auto-merged into the rendered doc; (d) refreshed via hourly planner or daily cron skill; (e) Evangelist bot reads HIDDEN_GEMS.md as input for blog/evangelism content (closes the loop with META-066).
  acceptance_criteria:
    - "docs/HIDDEN_GEMS.md exists with four structured sections: CLI commands, agent tools (MCP), config knobs (env vars), hidden features (workflow tricks)"
    - "Each entry has fields: name, where_to_find (file path), when_to_use (one-line value prop), example_command (copy-pasteable)"
    - scripts/dev/build-hidden-gems.sh auto-generates baseline doc from chump skill list, scripts/README.md catalog, chump-mcp.json server descriptions, and EVENT_REGISTRY.yaml ambient kinds
    - docs/HIDDEN_GEMS_CURATED.yaml is the operator overlay for hand-picked entries; build script merges curated overlay on top of auto-detected baseline so manual highlights survive regeneration
    - Refreshed automatically via daily cron skill OR hourly planner (whichever lower-cost); emits kind=hidden_gems_refreshed with delta count
    - Content Bot Evangelist (META-066) declares HIDDEN_GEMS.md as input data source in its system prompt — closes the discovery-to-evangelism loop
    - "CI test scripts/ci/test-hidden-gems-schema.sh: assert every entry has all four required fields, every where_to_find path resolves to a real file, no broken example_command references"
    - cargo fmt/clippy clean (script is shell but invokes Rust binary chump for chump skill list parsing) per CLAUDE.md local-CI discipline
  notes: |
    Pillar: CREDIBLE — discoverability is a measurement-of-trust signal (operators trust what they can find). Maps to multi-agent-factory pattern Phase 3: "Highlight hidden gems... package these findings into scenarios that show developers how they can reuse these primitives." Pairs with META-066 (Evangelist runtime consumes this doc), INFRA-1729 (capabilities registry — the machine-readable cousin of this human-readable doc). Without this, the Evangelist bot has nothing to evangelize about — it would re-discover primitives every run.
