- id: INFRA-2095
  domain: INFRA
  title: "GitHub native merge queue: batch N PRs in 1 CI cycle instead of N cycles — eliminates today's rebase-cascade whack-a-mole class entirely"
  status: done
  priority: P1
  effort: m
  description: |
    Enable GitHub native merge queue on main branch. Currently each PR gets its own full CI cycle; with merge queue, GitHub batches PRs into a single test run, only the batch needs to pass for all included PRs to merge. Eliminates today's rebase-cascade whack-a-mole class (where wedging one PR's merge cascade-blocks every subsequent PR). 47-PR day → ~10 batches instead of 47 cycles. Pairs with INFRA-2093 + INFRA-2094 for compounding speedup.
  acceptance_criteria:
    - GitHub branch protection on main has 'Require merge queue' enabled
    - ".github/workflows/ci.yml adds 'merge_group:' event trigger so CI runs on the merge-queue commit (not just push/pull_request)"
    - Per-PR CI continues to run for early feedback; merge-queue CI is the authoritative gate
    - "Auto-merge integration verified: PR with auto-merge armed + passing per-PR CI gets added to merge queue automatically"
    - "Batch failure handling tested: synth a batch with 1 failing PR + 1 passing PR, verify GitHub auto-bisects and ships the passing one"
    - Update docs/process/MERGE_QUEUE.md with operator-facing 'how merge queue works, what changes for me, how to bypass for emergencies'
    - "Measurement: before/after PR-to-merge wall-clock on a representative wave of 5 PRs"
  closed_date: '2026-05-29'
  closed_pr: 2687
  outcome_id: MISSION-010

