- id: INFRA-2269
  domain: INFRA
  title: "EFFECTIVE: chump keys — per-org Anthropic + GitHub key vault with scope isolation (encrypted local store; scope precedence repo>user>org>global; multi-tenant substrate prerequisite)"
  status: blocked
  priority: P2
  effort: m
  description: |
    Filed 2026-05-30. Env-var BYOK (CHUMP_AUTH_MODE + ANTHROPIC_API_KEY + CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN) works for single-operator. For paying-customer / multi-org scope (multi-tenant consumer surfaces), need per-org key vault with scope isolation. Substrate-layer primitive; vault lives in Chump, consumer surfaces call into it.
  acceptance_criteria:
    - "chump keys add <key-name> --value <value> --scope <global|org|user|repo> [--org NAME | --repo PATH]: stores in encrypted local vault; value never echoed to stdout/stderr/logs"
    - "chump keys list [--scope X] [--json]: shows key-name + scope + created-ts + last-accessed-ts (NEVER values); --json for machine output; default human table"
    - "chump keys get <key-name> [--scope X]: retrieves value; if vault encrypted with passphrase, gated by passphrase prompt (with CHUMP_VAULT_PASSPHRASE env var bypass for CI/scripts)"
    - "chump keys remove <key-name> --scope X: removes from vault; emits kind=key_removed (fields: key_name_hash, scope)"
