- id: INFRA-2304
  domain: INFRA
  title: "RESILIENT P0: disk_critical event → reactive escalation wiring — alarm fires but no consumer escalates reaper aggression or pages operator (today's 95% surprise)"
  status: done
  priority: P1
  effort: s
  description: |
    Operator real-talk 2026-05-30: "WTF is this happening... we should not ever have
    these surprises. Are we not wired up to automate this?"
    
    The fleet HAS every primitive needed but they are not wired end-to-end:
    
      EMITTER (works):    disk-health-monitor (5min cron) → emits disk_critical to ambient.jsonl
      EMITTER (works):    disk-pressure-watchdog (15min cron) → emits disk_critical to ambient.jsonl
      REAPER  (works):    disk-pressure-reaper --execute (15min cron) → tier 1-4 escalation
      PAUSER  (works):    worker.sh line 656 pauses on disk_critical
      PAUSER  (works):    chump gap reserve blocks on slo_breach
      PAGER   (exists):   scripts/dispatch/operator-recall.sh — halt-class pager
      ────────────────────── BREAKS HERE ──────────────────────
      disk_critical event has ZERO ambient consumers that ACT on it
      reaper runs on a FIXED 15min cron, not reactive to the alert
      operator-recall halt-classes don't include DISK_CRITICAL (only AUTH_DEAD,
        COST_CAP, CI_BROKEN, QUEUE_STARVE)
      reaper Tier 4 comment says "fall back to operator escalation" — no code path
    
    Result: between an ALERT at 16:45:47Z and the next 15min cron tick, nothing
    happens. Operator finds out because they happen to be in session. Today's
    incident: 95-98% disk, two ALERTs, manual operator triage required, ship-rate
    risk on every active claim.
    
    This is the META-128 "pre-action disk planning" gap's twin: META-128 plans
    BEFORE; this gap REACTS DURING. Both are needed.
  acceptance_criteria:
    - "New scripts/coord/disk-critical-reactor.sh: tails ambient.jsonl, on every disk_critical event invokes disk-pressure-reaper.sh --execute with tier forced to (current_tier + 1) — bounded by tier 4. De-bounced 60s per event to avoid thrash."
    - Launchd plist dev.chump.disk-critical-reactor.plist runs the reactor as a long-lived process (KeepAlive=true).
    - "operator-recall.sh gains DISK_CRITICAL halt-class: triggered when disk_critical fires AND post-reactor disk still <5% free for >10min. Reuses existing pager mechanism (ambient kind=operator_recall + optional POST to CHUMP_OPERATOR_RECALL_URL)."
    - "disk-pressure-reaper.sh Tier 4 (<5GB): replace the dead 'operator escalation' comment with an actual operator-recall.sh --condition DISK_CRITICAL invocation."
    - "Smoke test scripts/ci/test-disk-critical-reactor.sh: synthesize disk_critical event in temp ambient.jsonl; assert reactor invokes reaper with tier-up flag within 5s; assert idempotence inside the 60s debounce window."
    - Depends_on INFRA-2303 (sccache + incremental reapers) so the escalation has actual recoverable bytes to reap at tier 3-4.
  depends_on: [INFRA-2303]
