- id: INFRA-2724
  domain: INFRA
  title: "MISSION-EFFECTIVE: pillar starved — only 0 pickable xs/s/m gaps as of 2026-06-04"
  status: open
  priority: P3
  effort: s
  description: |
    In the `check_pillar_coverage` function, harden the EFFECTIVE-pillar gap-availability check so that it independently counts pickable xs, s, and m gaps instead of treating EFFECTIVE as a single coarse outcome. When any size (xs/s/m) returns zero available gaps, the function must emit a distinct starvation signal per missing size and exit non-zero.
    
    Target file(s):
    - scripts/coord/fleet-doctor-strict.sh
    
    (Spec enriched by chump-gap-enricher — EFFECTIVE-446. Original filer context preserved below.)
  acceptance_criteria:
    - "Run `scripts/coord/fleet-doctor-strict.sh` on a dataset dated ≥ 2026-06-04 and capture stdout; the line beginning 'EFFECTIVE-xs-pickable:' appears and reports >=1 when xs-sized EFFECTIVE gaps are available, otherwise 0."
    - "The same script log contains the lines 'EFFECTIVE-s-pickable:' and 'EFFECTIVE-m-pickable:' with independent counts; all three sizes must be >=1 for the final exit code to be 0."
    - In `src/web_server.rs`, the `/health/pillars` endpoint response body includes the JSON array `effective_starved_sizes` listing only the sizes (xs/s/m) whose pickable count is 0; the array is empty when all three sizes are present.
  opened_date: '2026-07-26'
  outcome_id: MISSION-010

- id: INFRA-2725
  domain: INFRA
  title: "MISSION-CREDIBLE: pillar starved — only 0 pickable xs/s/m gaps as of 2026-06-04"
  status: open
  priority: P3
  effort: s
  description: |
    Modify the gap selection queries in the main() functions of _pick_gap.py and _pick_and_claim_gap.py to include gaps tagged with the CREDIBLE pillar and size xs/s/m. Currently, these gaps are excluded because the pillar filter only matches a hardcoded list that omits CREDIBLE, or the size classification for CREDIBLE gaps is not being applied. The edit ensures that when the picker is invoked for the CREDIBLE pillar, it finds and returns at least 3 pickable gaps of those sizes.
    
    Target file(s):
    - scripts/dispatch/_pick_gap.py
    - scripts/dispatch/_pick_and_claim_gap.py
    
    (Spec enriched by chump-gap-enricher — EFFECTIVE-446. Original filer context preserved below.)
  acceptance_criteria:
    - Run `python scripts/dispatch/_pick_gap.py --pillar CREDIBLE --size xs,s,m --dry-run` and confirm the output lists >=3 distinct gap IDs.
    - Query `GET /health/pillars` (handled by handle_health_pillars in src/web_server.rs) and verify that the JSON field `CREDIBLE.pickable_xs_s_m` is an integer >=3.
    - Execute `scripts/coord/fleet-doctor-strict.sh` and check that it exits with code 0 and does not print 'CREDIBLE pillar starved' to stderr.
  opened_date: '2026-07-26'
  outcome_id: MISSION-010

- id: INFRA-2726
  domain: INFRA
  title: "MISSION-RESILIENT: pillar starved — only 0 pickable xs/s/m gaps as of 2026-06-04"
  status: open
  priority: P3
  effort: s
  description: |
    In scripts/coord/opus-curator.sh, modify the curator_decisions function to enforce a minimum of 3 pickable xs, s, or m gaps for the RESILIENT pillar after each decomposition cycle, by adding a post-check that re-triggers decomposition for that pillar if the count drops below 3.
    
    Target file(s):
