- id: INFRA-2786
  domain: INFRA
  title: "MISSION-EFFECTIVE: pillar starved — only 0 pickable xs/s/m gaps as of 2026-06-06"
  status: open
  priority: P3
  effort: s
  description: |
    Modify the `curator_decisions` function in scripts/coord/opus-curator.sh to detect when the EFFECTIVE pillar has fewer than three pickable gaps of sizes xs, s, or m. When this starvation condition is detected, the function will emit additional task-decomposition commands to generate at least three pickable gaps of each deficient size. Update the `run_curator` test in scripts/ci/test-curator-auto-decompose.sh with a `test_starvation_mitigation` case that seeds an empty pillar, runs the curator, and asserts the pickable gap counts become >=3 for each size.
    
    Target file(s):
    - scripts/coord/opus-curator.sh
    - scripts/ci/test-curator-auto-decompose.sh
    
    (Spec enriched by chump-gap-enricher — EFFECTIVE-446. Original filer context preserved below.)
  acceptance_criteria:
    - "Run `./scripts/ci/test-curator-auto-decompose.sh`; the `test_starvation_mitigation` scenario must pass, showing `run_curator` exits 0 and a subsequent `op query gaps --pillar EFFECTIVE --size xs,s,m --status pickable --count` returns `xs: >=3, s: >=3, m: >=3`."
    - Invoke `bash scripts/coord/opus-curator.sh` with a fixture database containing 0 EFFECTIVE xs, s, m gaps; after execution, verify that the curator log contains the string `Decomposed starvation gap for size xs` (and similarly for s, m) and that querying the gap pool confirms at least three new pickable gaps per size.
    - "Hit the health endpoint `GET /health/pillars` on the staging web service after the curator fix; the response body must show `effective_starved: false` and the `effective_pickable_counts` map must have values `xs>=3, s>=3, m>=3`."
  opened_date: '2026-07-26'
  outcome_id: MISSION-010

- id: INFRA-2787
  domain: INFRA
  title: "MISSION-CREDIBLE: pillar starved — only 0 pickable xs/s/m gaps as of 2026-06-06"
  status: open
  priority: P3
  effort: s
  description: |
    Modify the `main` function in both `_pick_gap.py` and `_pick_and_claim_gap.py` to filter candidate gaps by the CREDIBLE pillar, ensuring that the picker only considers xs, s, or m gaps belonging to that pillar; if no such gaps exist, emit a starvation signal instead of picking nothing.
    
    Target file(s):
    - scripts/dispatch/_pick_gap.py
    - scripts/dispatch/_pick_and_claim_gap.py
    
    (Spec enriched by chump-gap-enricher — EFFECTIVE-446. Original filer context preserved below.)
