- id: INFRA-2997
  domain: INFRA
  title: "RESILIENT: delete haiku downgrade routes (xs/s) — flat subscription makes cost argument invalid, haiku 0% ship rate today"
  status: done
  priority: P0
  effort: xs
  description: |
    RESILIENT: Delete the effort:xs and effort:s routes (model_class: haiku) from docs/dispatch/routing.yaml. With no matching route, scripts/dispatch/_resolve_model.py returns its fallback (worker base FLEET_MODEL, default sonnet per worker.sh:117). Root cause: INFRA-515 flipped the default haiku->sonnet at worker.sh:1017, but routing SETS FLEET_MODEL=haiku at worker.sh:719 BEFORE that guard, making ${FLEET_MODEL-sonnet} a no-op for every xs/s pick. 2026-06-21 data: 32 haiku spawns, 6 cycle_stall_killed, 0 real ships 18:00-20:00Z (haiku runs cargo check on shell gaps -> 2-5min recompile -> exceeds 120s INFRA-705 stall threshold). Flat Claude subscription => no per-token cost delta => 'save tokens' rationale invalid. Shape: (a) remove both route blocks in routing.yaml, (b) update header comment + add INFRA-2997/INFRA-515 justification comment, (c) update scripts/ci/test-model-class-routing.sh assertions xs/s haiku->sonnet. Do NOT change m/l/xl routes, cognition/research routes, or worker.sh.
  acceptance_criteria:
    - "The 'match: { effort: xs }' route (model_class: haiku) is removed from docs/dispatch/routing.yaml"
    - "The 'match: { effort: s }' route (model_class: haiku) is removed from docs/dispatch/routing.yaml"
    - _resolve_model.py returns 'sonnet' (not 'haiku') for xs and s effort gaps when FLEET_MODEL fallback is sonnet
    - m/l/xl routes and cognition/research routes still resolve to sonnet (no regression)
    - scripts/ci/test-model-class-routing.sh passes with updated xs->sonnet and s->sonnet assertions
  notes: |
    SUPERSEDED by RESILIENT-154 (PR #3146 'remove haiku from the fleet — sonnet is the floor', merged to origin/main 2026-06-21). RESILIENT-154 achieves the identical outcome (xs/s effort -> model_class sonnet, no haiku stalls) by flipping the routes rather than deleting them. Filed/claimed/implemented INFRA-2997 (route deletion) in parallel; standing down rather than unilaterally revert a merged sibling change (CLAUDE.md: route routing/doctrine changes through consensus). Same-day haiku-removal sweep: MISSION-047 #3142, MISSION-048 #3145, RESILIENT-154 #3146.
  closed_pr: 3227
  outcome_id: MISSION-010

- id: INFRA-2998
  domain: INFRA
  title: "RESILIENT: all-sonnet fleet orphans xs gaps — sonnet refuses xs at _pick_gap.py:470, but flat subscription makes that gate invalid too (sibling of INFRA-2997)"
  status: done
  priority: P1
  effort: s
  description: |
    Sibling of INFRA-2997. The picker gate at scripts/dispatch/_pick_gap.py:470 makes a sonnet worker REFUSE effort=xs gaps (unless P0-MISSION). That gate assumed a MIXED fleet where haiku workers handle xs/s. But run-fleet.sh:268 defaults FLEET_MODEL=sonnet (the L38 'default haiku' comment is stale), so the real fleet is all-sonnet — and INFRA-2997 removed the last path that put xs work on haiku. Net: regular (non-P0-MISSION) xs gaps now have NO worker. The same flat-subscription reasoning that voided the xs/s haiku routes (no per-token cost delta; sonnet ships, haiku stalls at 1/9 per INFRA-515) voids the 'don't burn frontier tokens on xs' rationale behind this gate. Fix: drop or flag-gate the sonnet-refuses-xs check so sonnet workers pick xs. Out of scope for INFRA-2997 (that PR was routing.yaml-only).
  acceptance_criteria:
    - scripts/dispatch/_pick_gap.py no longer makes sonnet workers unconditionally refuse effort=xs (gate removed or behind a mixed-fleet opt-in flag)
    - A sonnet worker picks an xs gap in a default all-sonnet fleet (demonstrated via _pick_gap.py with FLEET_MODEL=sonnet on an xs fixture)
    - scripts/ci/test-model-class-routing.sh sonnet-refuses-xs assertion updated to match the new behavior
    - "run-fleet.sh:38 stale 'default haiku' comment corrected to reflect the sonnet default at L268"
  closed_pr: 3227
  outcome_id: MISSION-010

