- id: INFRA-3403
  domain: INFRA
  title: "RESILIENT: restore remaining self-hosted runner lanes (AUDIT/COVERAGE/E2E_GOLDEN_PATH/TAURI) one at a time"
  status: done
  priority: P2
  effort: m
  description: |
    Follow-up from INFRA-1655. Root cause of the 2026-05-20 self-hosted-runner
    "checkout flake" was identified: pre-INFRA-1852 concurrency-group keying
    (by PR number, fixed to github.sha in PR #2446) caused GitHub to cancel
    in-flight self-hosted jobs on every fixup push, producing 0-step CANCELLED
    failures that looked like a checkout flake. That bug is fixed on main.
    
    RUNNER_E2E_PWA was restored as the canary lane on 2026-07-22
    (gh variable set RUNNER_E2E_PWA --body '["self-hosted","macos-arm64","chump-fleet"]').
    
    This gap restores the remaining 4 lanes ONE AT A TIME, waiting for a clean
    PR cycle after each, per docs/process/SELF_HOSTED_RUNNERS.md "Remaining steps":
      1. RUNNER_AUDIT
      2. RUNNER_COVERAGE
      3. RUNNER_E2E_GOLDEN_PATH
      4. RUNNER_TAURI_COWORK_E2E
    Do not batch — if one lane flakes, you need to know which.
  acceptance_criteria:
    - "1. Confirm RUNNER_E2E_PWA canary has run clean (no CANCELLED/checkout-fail) across >=3 PR cycles\n2. Restore RUNNER_AUDIT, wait one clean PR cycle\n3. Restore RUNNER_COVERAGE, wait one clean PR cycle\n4. Restore RUNNER_E2E_GOLDEN_PATH and RUNNER_TAURI_COWORK_E2E, wait one clean PR cycle\n5. Update docs/process/SELF_HOSTED_RUNNERS.md \"Repo variable state\" table to reflect final state\n6. Emit ambient kind=runner_health_restored on full restoration"
  notes: |
    [2026-08-31T08:12:33Z] CREDIBLE-178: closed via PR #4340 with UNCOVERED acceptance criteria "misses":[0]. Verify the work is complete before trusting status=done.
  opened_date: '2026-07-26'
  closed_date: '2026-08-31'
  closed_pr: 4340

