- id: INFRA-3474
  domain: INFRA
  title: "RESILIENT: outward-flywheel execution is BLOCKED — chump improve requires the claude CLI (not installed); no chump-local external-repo path"
  status: done
  priority: P1
  effort: m
  description: |
    STRATEGIC (operator 2026-07-28): the OS must NEVER default to the claude CLI — it contradicts 'own your tools' + the swappable-harness design + the shared-service discipline. External-repo execution must DEFAULT to chump-local (ProviderCascade), claude CLI opt-in.
    
    CONFIRMED BLOCKER (scoped in worktree): execute_gap conflates gap-source and file-root. It reads the gap via repo_path::main_checkout_root() (git-common-dir from repo_root, which follows CHUMP_REPO/cwd) AND roots the agent's file tools at the same CHUMP_REPO. External work needs them DECOUPLED: gap from chump's canonical state.db, files in the external clone. Setting CHUMP_REPO=clone breaks gap lookup (looks in almanac's state.db → INFRA-3468 not found). So it's a refactor, not a flag.
    
    RECOMMENDED APPROACH A (cleanest, testable, reuses improve's contract): add a 'chump agent-run --prompt-file <f> [--cwd <dir>] [--model <class>]' subcommand that runs the chump-local ChumpAgent (build_chump_agent_cli → ProviderCascade, DEFAULT all-tools profile incl git_push/gh) on an ad-hoc prompt in cwd — NO gap lookup, so no conflation. Then improve.rs implement_gap gets CHUMP_IMPROVE_BACKEND (default 'chump-local'): spawn 'chump agent-run --prompt-file <improve's ExternalRepoContract prompt> --cwd <clone>' instead of 'claude -p'; the agent implements+commits+pushes+opens the PR per the existing contract prompt; improve extracts pr_url same as today. claude path becomes opt-in (CHUMP_IMPROVE_BACKEND=claude). Also fix: improve --gap must ensure the clone exists (scout is skipped). PART 1 (built, not yet shipped): execute_gap CHUMP_EXECUTE_GAP_NO_SHIP edit-only mode — keep for approach B or drop.
    
    APPROACH B (bigger): give execute_gap external-repo awareness (separate CHUMP_GAP_SOURCE root from CHUMP_REPO file-root) + improve branch/push/PR orchestration. More invasive.
    
    This is the mission's critical execution path — build carefully, test the external PR end-to-end before trusting. Reconcile: how does BEAST-MODE ship today (claude CLI on another machine?).
  acceptance_criteria:
    - "The change described by \"outward-flywheel execution is BLOCKED — chump improve requires the claude CLI (not installed); no chump-local external-repo path\" is implemented in the relevant INFRA code path(s)."
    - At least one test (cargo test or scripts/ci/test-*.sh) proves the new behavior and fails without the change.
