- id: INFRA-3516
  domain: INFRA
  title: "COTG-1.3: remediation/fix_pr commit path bypasses deterministic_ship guards (junk-exclusion + verify_staged_edit)"
  status: done
  priority: P1
  effort: s
  description: |
    The external-improve flow applies its reliability guards ASYMMETRICALLY. The initial
    ship (deterministic_ship, COTG-1.2/1.3) resets runtime junk (.chump-locks/, sessions/,
    .chump/) out of the index and runs verify_staged_edit (destructive-clobber + invalid
    JSON/TOML/YAML rejection) before committing. But the no-abandon remediation path
    (remediate_held -> fix_pr -> AgentFix) commits with its own raw `git add -A` + commit
    and applies NEITHER guard. So a PR that starts clean gets corrupted by its own
    remediation loop: runtime junk leaks in and destructive edits go unchecked.
  acceptance_criteria:
    - fix_pr / remediation commits route through the SAME guarded ceremony as the initial ship (junk-exclusion reset + verify_staged_edit) — ideally a shared helper both call, not two copies.
    - a remediation commit that would clobber (numstat deletion>=50 && insertion*10<deletion) is rejected, exactly as the ship path rejects it.
    - runtime junk (.chump-locks/, sessions/, .chump/, *.db / *.db-shm / *.db-wal) never appears in a remediation commit's diff.
    - regression test — a remediate run over a clone that has runtime junk on disk produces a clean cumulative PR diff (0 junk files) across ALL commits, not just the first.
  notes: |
    [2026-08-20T00:00:00Z] RECONCILE: already shipped via b344ae92 (PR #3396,
    "fix(INFRA-3516): guarded remediation ceremony (re-land, rebased+clippy-clean)"),
    preceded by 6fea9e55/741f365f. src/improve.rs now has guarded_stage_and_commit()
    as the ONE staging+commit ceremony shared by deterministic_ship (initial ship)
    and fix_pr_dispatch (remediation path) — junk-exclusion reset + verify_staged_edit
    + verify_not_stub all run on both paths. Regression coverage:
    guarded_commit_drops_junk_and_rejects_clobber test at src/improve.rs:5382. All 4
    AC bullets met. Gap YAML was left status:open in this worktree only — state.db
    has no open row for it (chump gap ship already run, closed_pr=3396).
  closed_pr: 3396
  evidence: |
    PROVEN 2026-07-29 running `chump improve repairman29/BEAST-MODE --apply` (binary built
    from origin/main 57518ed5, floor present). The OS autonomously picked a REAL gap
    ("Install PM2 / fix failing CI"), opened trailered zero-touch PR #35, then verify-merge
    HELD it and ran no-abandon remediation (sonnet->opus, NO claude spawn — Principle-0 held).
    Per-commit junk analysis of PR #35 (branch chump/improve-p94851):
      commit 1  ebf0ad6a (deterministic_ship path)  -> 0 junk files   [guard worked]
      commit 2  fc3ae28d (remediation/fix_pr path)   -> 4 junk files   [guard bypassed]
      commit 3  66a2e3d9 (remediation/fix_pr path)   -> 3 junk files   [guard bypassed]
    Cumulative diff also shows package.json at +6/-324 — a deletion the verify_staged_edit
    clobber heuristic (d>=50 && a*10<d) WOULD have rejected on the ship path, but the
    remediation path never runs it. Root cause: the guards live inside deterministic_ship,
    not in a helper shared by fix_pr's commit path.

