- id: INFRA-3540
  domain: INFRA
  title: "audit.yml has no docs-only lane: a 3-file .md PR pays two full cargo builds (~4.5m each) for gates that test nothing it changed"
  status: blocked
  priority: P2
  effort: s
  acceptance_criteria:
    - "MEASURED 2026-08-08 on audit run 31266833185 (green, main). Shard wall-clock: shard-1 7m, shard-4 6m, shard-2 1m, shard-3 1m. Critical path = shard-1, and audit is the floor on EVERY PR including doc-only ones (see EFFECTIVE-415)"
    - THE COST IS ONE COMPILE, NOT THE GATES. shard-1's slowest step is 'chump gap list domain summary (INFRA-431)' at 239s and shard-4's is 'stale-binary destructive-op guard (INFRA-825)' at 268s. Both are simply the FIRST step in their shard to run 'cargo build --bin chump' so each absorbs the whole cold compile; every later cargo step in the same shard is 1-2s. INFRA-582's own comment on that step claims 'Debug with shared cache completes in <60s' — it is 4x that now, so the comment is stale and should be corrected in the same change
    - "DO NOT REBALANCE THE SHARDS. The 7/6/1/1 imbalance looks like the bug and is not: shards 1 and 4 are slow because they compile, not because they hold more gates. Their gates are cargo-dependent and cannot move to shards 2/3, which have no binary. Redistributing gates would cost effort and save zero wall-clock. This is written down so the obvious-looking fix is not attempted"
    - "THE ACTUAL FIX — a docs-only lane in audit.yml. It currently has NO path filtering whatsoever (on: push/pull_request with no paths-ignore and no lane job). ci.yml already computes lane outputs and gates 3 jobs on 'rust'. When a PR changes zero .rs / .toml / .sh / gap-YAML files, the cargo gates in shards 1 and 4 verify binary behavior the PR cannot have altered — skip them"
    - "SAFETY IS NON-NEGOTIABLE AND THE PATTERN ALREADY EXISTS: audit is branch-protection required, so skipping must use the needs + if:always() aggregator so 'audit' and 'audit-required' still report SUCCESS on a skipped lane. This is proven in-repo — clippy-required and cargo-test-required did exactly this on PR #3489 while their lanes skipped. Do not invent a new mechanism"
    - "SCOPE THE LANE NARROWLY: Chump gaps are YAML, so 'documentation' is NOT the test — gap-integrity and gap-status gates MUST still run whenever any gap YAML changes. Gate on 'touched only docs/**/*.md and no .rs/.toml/.sh/gap YAML', and prove it with a fixture PR that touches a gap YAML and confirms the cargo gates still fire"
    - "SEPARATE, SMALLER LEVER (file as follow-up if it does not fit here): sccache hit rate is 31% on that run — 901 compile requests, 714 executed, only 281 hits. Improving it cuts BOTH build shards on every PR, including the Rust PRs a docs-only lane can never help. Record the hit rate in the run so it is trendable rather than rediscovered"
  notes: |
    [2026-08-29T02:54:30Z] INFRA-3832 auto-block: 3 consecutive non-ship cycles (last kind=rc=1, rc=1, cycle_log=0B). Worker kept re-picking + looping; blocked to leave the pick pool. Un-block after fixing the spec / decomposing.
  opened_date: '2026-08-19'
  outcome_id: MISSION-010

- id: INFRA-3541
  domain: INFRA
  title: "pre-push CI-regression guard crashes with 'GUARD_SCRIPTS[@]: unbound variable' — it fails open on exactly the pushes it guards"
  status: blocked
  priority: P2
  effort: s
  acceptance_criteria:
    - "OBSERVED 2026-08-08 pushing a ci.yml change to chump/effective-396-claim. The hook printed '[ci-regression-guard] ci.yml changed in this push — checking CI-Regression-Guard trailers.' and then immediately 'scripts/git-hooks/pre-push-ci-regression-guard.sh: line 172: GUARD_SCRIPTS[@]: unbound variable'. The push SUCCEEDED"
    - "THE FAILURE MODE IS FAIL-OPEN, WHICH IS THE WORST ONE FOR A GUARD: it announces that it is checking, crashes, and lets the push through anyway. Anyone reading the output sees the reassuring first line. The guard has therefore been inert on ci.yml pushes for however long this has been broken, while appearing to run"
    - "CAUSE is almost certainly bash 'set -u' plus an EMPTY array — in bash < 4.4 (and macOS ships 3.2) an empty array expanded as  is treated as unbound rather than empty. Fix with ${GUARD_SCRIPTS[@]+\"${GUARD_SCRIPTS[@]}\"} or by seeding the array, at scripts/git-hooks/pre-push-ci-regression-guard.sh:172"
    - DECIDE FAIL-OPEN VS FAIL-CLOSED DELIBERATELY and write the choice into the script as a comment. A guard that cannot run should probably block the push and say so, but that is a judgement call about developer friction — the current behaviour is not a choice, it is an accident
    - "VERIFY on both bash 3.2 (macOS default, /bin/bash) and bash 5.x: push a ci.yml change with no CI-Regression-Guard trailer and assert the guard actually evaluates rather than crashing. A regression test belongs in scripts/ci/ alongside the other hook tests"
    - "Found while unblocking PR #3509 (EFFECTIVE-396). Not filed as part of that PR because it is an unrelated pre-existing defect in a different script"
  notes: |
    [2026-08-29T02:54:42Z] INFRA-3832 auto-block: 3 consecutive non-ship cycles (last kind=rc=1, rc=1, cycle_log=0B). Worker kept re-picking + looping; blocked to leave the pick pool. Un-block after fixing the spec / decomposing.
