    - "THE RISK IS LIVE THE MOMENT A CONSUMER IS WIRED. Nothing consumes stale_post_merge_gap today, so the repair holds. CREDIBLE-275 asks for consumers to be wired for events that have none — doing that without fixing this first could RE-CLOSE the gaps we just recovered. Sequence matters: fix this before wiring that consumer"
    - "THERE IS NO SUPPORTED WAY TO CLEAR IT: chump gap set --closed-pr rejects an empty value (\"expects a positive integer\"), no --clear-closed-pr exists, and direct sqlite UPDATE is correctly refused by tooling policy since it bypasses CLI invariants"
