- id: INFRA-3618
  domain: INFRA
  title: "Substrate S1: shadow dual-write chump-gap-store to self-hosted shared_gaps (best-effort, reads unchanged, reversible) — first safe stage of the one-canonical-store permanent fix"
  status: open
  priority: P2
  effort: m
  description: |
    PERMANENT FIX for the gap-store split-brain. Staged, each stage individually safe + reversible; next stage filed only after prior verified live. S0 (DONE): self-hosted Postgres + PostgREST on CJ, shared_gaps/shared_claims(CAS)/worker_capabilities schema applied. S1 (THIS): write-only shadow — mutations dual-write to shared_gaps, reads unchanged. S2: parity validator gates >=99.x% for K days. S3: flip reads behind CHUMP_STORE_BACKEND=postgres, canary one node, CAS claims via shared_claims. S4: retire yaml, state.db becomes read-through cache, coherence reconcilers become unnecessary. S5: SPOF hardening — backup/restore + graceful degrade to state.db read-only if Postgres down.
  acceptance_criteria:
    - chump-gap-store depends on chump-team (PostgREST client); every gap mutation (reserve/set/claim/ship/close) additionally writes the row to shared_gaps on the self-hosted store
    - "SAFETY INVARIANT (blocking): the shadow write is best-effort — any failure (network/schema/timeout) is logged kind=shadow_write_failed and SWALLOWED; it MUST NOT block, add >250ms, or throw on the canonical state.db path. Canonical behavior is identical with shadow on or off"
    - Reads are UNCHANGED (still state.db) this stage — write-only shadow, zero read-path risk
    - Gated behind CHUMP_STORE_SHADOW=1 (default OFF); enabling it is logged to docs/process/CAPABILITY_DECISIONS.md as a tracked toggle
    - "CHUMP_TEAM_URL + CHUMP_TEAM_API_KEY wired into worker/CLI env on CJ pointing at the local PostgREST (:3000); documented in the PR"
    - scripts/coord/substrate-parity.sh reports row-count + per-field drift between state.db and shared_gaps (for the S2 gate)
    - "Reversible: CHUMP_STORE_SHADOW=0 fully disables with zero residue; rollback documented"
    - "Test: fault-injection — a mutation with the shadow store unreachable still succeeds on canonical + emits shadow_write_failed. VERIFY-LIVE: >=5 real gaps appear in shared_gaps after enabling on CJ. Depth tier + gaps named per green-not-covered"
  notes: |
    Decomposed into 9 slices: INFRA-6478, INFRA-6479, INFRA-6480, INFRA-6481, INFRA-6482, INFRA-6483, INFRA-6484, INFRA-6485, INFRA-6486
  opened_date: '2026-08-21'
  outcome_id: MISSION-010
  evidence: |
    COMMAND: stood up Postgres 18 + chump_fleet + PostgREST :3000 on CJ (chump-postgrest.service), proven gap insert/read round-trip. OUTPUT: split-brain today = 2 drifting state.db files (0-row machine-scope vs 4159-row repo-local) + 4139 retired yaml + state.sql dump, producing 50% reconcile-waste merges. THEORY: no loop derives gap-state from a single canonical store; every reconciler is bookkeeping that itself drifts. One canonical Postgres store removes the SOURCE. ALT: keep patching reconcilers (RESILIENT-194/364) — rejected, they ARE the drift they patch (this session's tragedy).

- id: INFRA-3619
  domain: INFRA
  title: "Gap Fairy: Wonka-gate intake assay + continuous backlog furnace — bad eggs never reach the pickable scale, and the dirty backlog is deduped/primed/furnaced automatically"
  status: blocked
  priority: P2
  effort: l
  description: |
    Sibling to Race Control (CREDIBLE-296, watches merges) and the RCA reflex (RESILIENT-365). Race Control watches the OUTPUT; the Gap Fairy guards the INTAKE. Built by orchestrating EXISTING tools (mine-before-build): gap triage (INFRA-942), decompose (LLM AC), dep-clean, consolidate (INFRA-935), audit-ac, rebalance — none of which today run continuously, furnace, or enforce admission.
  acceptance_criteria:
    - "ADMISSION GATE (file-time): a newly reserved gap lands as status=needs-prep (NOT ready/pickable) unless it passes the assay — concrete testable AC (not empty/TODO/vague per audit-ac), right-sized (not too-large), no false-deps, has outcome+evidence (already gated), and is not a near-duplicate of an existing open gap (consolidate check). A bad egg never reaches the pickable scale."
    - "FURNACE ORGAN (continuous timer): each cycle (1) DEDUP via consolidate — for each near-dup cluster keep the best gap (highest priority / most AC / oldest), migrate any unique AC, auto-close the losers status=closed reason=duplicate; (2) PRIME via decompose — vague-AC + empty-AC to tight AC, split too-large; promote fixed gaps to ready; (3) FURNACE the unsalvageable — stale/cruft/cannot-pass-after-N-attempts auto-close reason=furnaced with a stated reason."
    - "GUARDRAILS (furnace is destructive-ish): NEVER furnace P0/P1 (only P2/P3 cruft + confirmed dups); every auto-close is fully reversible via chump gap requeue (close != delete, honors archive-not-delete); daily furnace cap (env CHUMP_FAIRY_FURNACE_CAP default 50); dry-run mode; guarded behind CHUMP_GAP_FAIRY_ENABLED default OFF, logged to docs/process/CAPABILITY_DECISIONS.md as a tracked toggle."
    - "DETECTABLE: emits kind=gap_assay_report each cycle (primed N, deduped N, furnaced N, pickable-pool% = ready/open) so Race Control + the board see intake health. Wired as chump-gap-fairy.timer + .service + organ manifest (built+wired+detectable+revivable, Roll-Call)."
    - "PROOF: on the current live backlog it must collapse the 573 near-dup clusters and lift pickable-pool% measurably; test with a seeded dirty-backlog fixture asserts dups closed + vague-AC primed + P0/P1 never furnaced + a furnaced gap requeues cleanly. Depth tier + gaps named per green-not-covered. VERIFY-LIVE: chump-gap-fairy.timer is-active on CJ + one real gap_assay_report in ambient."
  notes: |
    Decomposed into 11 slices: INFRA-5781, INFRA-5782, INFRA-5783, INFRA-5784, INFRA-5785, INFRA-5786, INFRA-5787, INFRA-5788, INFRA-5789, INFRA-5790, INFRA-5791
    [2026-09-10T12:33:19Z] INFRA-3832 auto-block: 3 consecutive non-ship cycles (last kind=rc=1, rc=1, cycle_log=1419B). Worker kept re-picking + looping; blocked to leave the pick pool. Un-block after fixing the spec / decomposing.
  opened_date: '2026-08-21'
  outcome_id: MISSION-010
  evidence: |
    COMMAND: chump gap list/triage/consolidate/audit-ac on the live queue + gh pr list. OUTPUT: 1329 open gaps but only ~965 pickable — 364 non-pickable (110 vague-AC, 116 empty-AC, 43 too-large, 31 false-dep, 180 low-pri) AND 573 near-duplicate title clusters. Meanwhile only 4 open PRs + 2-4 merges/hr = CI has HEADROOM. THEORY: throughput is NOT CI-bound; it is bound by a dirty/unprimed queue — a bad egg wastes a worker's entire cycle (claim->fail->rework->unverified_ship->cooldown) when picked. Fix = a Willy-Wonka admission gate (bad eggs never reach the pickable scale) + a continuous furnace organ that dedups/primes/closes-unsalvageable, ORCHESTRATING existing tools (triage/decompose/dep-clean/consolidate) which today are manual+scattered with no furnace and no admission enforcement. ALT: keep manually running triage/decompose (what the board did this session) — rejected, not continuous, no furnace, backlog re-dirties.

