- id: INFRA-3678
  domain: INFRA
  title: agent_loop strip_prefix_caseless panics on non-char-boundary byte slice (crashes free-tier flash execute-gap)
  status: done
  priority: P1
  effort: xs
  description: |
    During EFFECTIVE-446 payoff run (2026-08-23), a free-tier flash execute-gap (INFRA-1318 on deepseek-v4-flash) PANICKED after making a valid str_replace edit: thread main panicked at src/agent_loop/types.rs:452:36 end byte index N is not a char boundary; it is inside a multi-byte char. Root cause: fn strip_prefix_caseless does s[..prefix.len()] (byte-index slice) with no char-boundary check; when s has a multibyte UTF-8 char straddling prefix.len(), the slice panics and crashes the whole execute-gap (exit 101). This intermittently kills the DeepSeek cheap-floor whenever model/file text contains multibyte chars, blocking the flash drain.
  acceptance_criteria:
    - In src/agent_loop/types.rs strip_prefix_caseless, replace the s[..prefix.len()] slice with a char-boundary-safe form (e.g. s.get(..prefix.len()) or an s.as_bytes() caseless compare) so a multibyte char at the boundary yields None instead of panicking.
  closed_date: '2026-08-23'
  closed_pr: 4188

