- id: INFRA-3832
  domain: INFRA
  title: "Worker never infinite-loops on a problematic gap: uniform non-ship cooldown + auto-block chronic offenders + tree-reap wedge kills"
  status: shipped
  priority: P1
  effort: m
  description: |
    Extend INFRA-3808 to ALL non-ship cycle outcomes. The INFRA-361 cooldown block lived only in the else (rc!=0 AND rc!=124) branch, so rc=124 timeouts/wedges (INFRA-3798, INFRA-1497) wrote no cooldown and were re-picked forever; watchdogs killed only the wrapper subshell, leaving claude orphaned until FLEET_TIMEOUT_S (66min). Fix: merge failure branches; escalating bounded backoff via a durable offense ledger; auto-block after N non-ship cycles (env-guarded); _kill_cycle_tree reaps the whole tree at both watchdog kill sites.
  acceptance_criteria:
    - Every non-ship cycle outcome (timeout rc=124, wedge, worker_timeout_no_commit, unverified_ship, rc-fail) writes a valid-JSON per-gap cooldown file the picker honors
    - A gap that wedges/times-out N times in a row is auto-set status=blocked (env-guarded) so it leaves the pick pool entirely
    - Watchdog kills reap the hung claude descendant tree so a 0B-log/no-progress hang is caught in ~120s not 66min
    - scripts/ci/test-infra-3832-*.sh proves the behavior and passes; worker.sh parses under bash -n
  opened_date: '2026-08-26'
  closed_pr: 4265

- id: INFRA-3833
  domain: INFRA
  title: "ZERO-WASTE: implement chump-github-cache refresh-open-prs bulk REST fill + divergence-audit infra (prereq for real INFRA-2062 cutover)"
  status: open
  priority: P2
  effort: m
  description: |
    INFRA-2062 investigation (2026-08-28) found the Phase 2 cutover premise unmet: neither the Python webhook receiver nor the Rust chump-webhook-receiver has ever run continuously in this environment (ps aux shows neither process alive, no launchd plist installed for either, .chump/github_cache.db does not even exist), no sqlite_diff/divergence-audit script exists, and refresh-open-prs is still an explicit Phase 1 stub (prints 0, no octocrab dep in Cargo.toml) per chump-github-cache/src/lib.rs's own doc comment: 'NO bulk-refill REST loop ... real refill comes in a follow-up sub-gap.' This gap is that follow-up: make refresh-open-prs functionally real and add divergence-tracking infra so a genuine 14-day parallel-run window (INFRA-2062 AC1) can actually start being measured, instead of being claimed without data.
  acceptance_criteria:
    - chump-github-cache-cli refresh-open-prs performs a real bulk REST refill (octocrab or reqwest, matching bash cache_refresh_open_prs semantics) instead of printing a stub 0
    - nightly divergence-audit script compares Python-receiver-written rows vs Rust-receiver-written rows for the same primary keys and emits ambient kind=cache_divergence_detected on any mismatch
