- id: INFRA-4760
  domain: INFRA
  title: "INFRA: Implement gap assay helper function (INFRA-3619 slice)"
  status: open
  priority: P2
  effort: xs
  acceptance_criteria:
    - "Function returns PASS/FAIL based on: non‑empty AC, right‑sized description, no false dependencies, presence of outcome+evidence, and not a near‑duplicate"
    - Unit tests cover each rule and edge cases
    - Function is pure and callable from other components

- id: INFRA-4761
  domain: INFRA
  title: "INFRA: Add admission gate to gap intake pipeline (INFRA-3619 slice)"
  status: open
  priority: P2
  effort: s
  acceptance_criteria:
    - When a new gap is reserved, the gate runs the assay function
    - If assay PASS, gap status is set to READY and is pickable
    - If assay FAIL, gap status is set to NEEDS-PREP and is not pickable
    - Gate execution is skipped when CHUMP_GAP_FAIRY_ENABLED is OFF
  depends_on: [INFRA-4760]

- id: INFRA-4762
  domain: INFRA
  title: "INFRA: Implement deduplication (consolidate) step (INFRA-3619 slice)"
  status: open
  priority: P2
  effort: s
  acceptance_criteria:
    - Runs after admission gate and identifies near‑duplicate clusters
    - Keeps the highest‑priority gap (or oldest with most AC) in each cluster
    - Auto‑closes other gaps with status=CLOSED and reason=DUPLICATE
    - Closed gaps retain full history for possible requeue
  depends_on: [INFRA-4761]

- id: INFRA-4763
  domain: INFRA
  title: "INFRA: Implement priming (decompose) step (INFRA-3619 slice)"
  status: open
  priority: P2
  effort: s
  acceptance_criteria:
    - Detects gaps with vague or empty AC and rewrites them to concrete AC
    - Splits gaps whose description exceeds size threshold into multiple child gaps
    - Promotes successfully primed gaps to status=READY
    - No gap is promoted without at least one concrete acceptance criterion
  depends_on: [INFRA-4762]

- id: INFRA-4764
  domain: INFRA
  title: "INFRA: Implement furnace unsalvageable step (INFRA-3619 slice)"
  status: open
  priority: P2
  effort: s
  acceptance_criteria:
    - Gaps that remain in NEEDS-PREP after N (configurable) attempts are auto‑closed with reason=FURNACED
    - P0 and P1 gaps are never auto‑closed by this step
    - Closed gaps are reversible via the chump‑gap requeue command
    - Furnace respects daily cap defined by CHUMP_FAIRY_FURNACE_CAP
  depends_on: [INFRA-4763]

- id: INFRA-4765
  domain: INFRA
  title: "INFRA: Add guardrails around furnace operation (INFRA-3619 slice)"
  status: open
  priority: P2
  effort: s
  acceptance_criteria:
    - Dry‑run mode (CHUMP_FAIRY_DRY_RUN) logs intended closures without performing them
    - Daily furnace cap is enforced and logged
    - Attempt to furnace a P0/P1 gap results in a warning and no action
    - All auto‑close actions are recorded in audit log for later requeue
  depends_on: [INFRA-4764]

- id: INFRA-4766
  domain: INFRA
  title: "INFRA: Create systemd timer and service (chump-gap-fairy.timer/.service) (INFRA-3619 slice)"
  status: open
  priority: P2
  effort: s
  acceptance_criteria:
    - Timer triggers the fairy service at the configured interval (default 1h)
    - Service executes the full intake → dedup → prime → furnace pipeline
    - Service exits with status 0 on success and logs errors on failure
    - Service is disabled by default and enabled only when CHUMP_GAP_FAIRY_ENABLED=ON
  depends_on: [INFRA-4765]

- id: INFRA-4767
  domain: INFRA
  title: "INFRA: Emit gap_assay_report event each cycle (INFRA-3619 slice)"
  status: open
  priority: P2
  effort: xs
  acceptance_criteria:
    - After each timer run, a JSON event of kind=gap_assay_report is published to the event bus
    - "Event includes counts: primed, deduped, furnaced, and current pickable‑pool percentage"
    - Race Control can consume the event and display health metrics
    - Event schema is documented in docs/events.md
  depends_on: [INFRA-4766]

