- id: INFRA-823
  domain: INFRA
  title: "ZERO-WASTE: shipped-but-not-closed gaps accumulate — bot-merge.sh does not auto-close gap YAML on merge"
  status: done
  priority: P1
  effort: s
  description: |
    As of 2026-05-11, at least 3 gaps have code merged to main but YAML still shows status:open:
    - INFRA-816: fixed in PR #1437 (fix(infra-816): add system deps to release-plz.yml) — gap still open
    - CREDIBLE-013: shipped in PR #1431 (CREDIBLE-013: CI failure triage) — gap still open
    - INFRA-817: fixed in PR #1442 (fix(e2e): update PWA v2 test selectors) — gap still open
    
    In addition, INFRA-796/797/798 have pr: 1421 set but status: open, indicating partial ship.
    
    The CLAUDE.md ship pipeline says to run `chump gap ship <ID> --update-yaml` after merge.
    Bot-merge.sh does not call this automatically. When the agent that shipped moves on to the
    next gap, the prior gap stays open forever unless someone manually closes it.
    
    This is pure waste: false signal in the open queue, incorrect pillar counts, and audit tools
    reporting on "open with closed_pr" pattern will eventually mis-report metrics.
  acceptance_criteria:
    - bot-merge.sh calls chump gap ship <GAP-ID> --update-yaml after successful gh pr merge
    - Gap ID extracted from branch name (pattern chump/<GAP-ID>-*) or PR title prefix
    - "chump gap audit-priorities \"open with closed_pr\" count = 0"
    - INFRA-816, CREDIBLE-013, INFRA-817 closed (or manually confirmed still incomplete)
    - scripts/ci/test-bot-merge-auto-close.sh verifies the new behavior on a fixture gap
  opened_date: '2026-05-11'
  closed_pr: 1490
  outcome_id: MISSION-010

- id: INFRA-824
  domain: INFRA
  title: "CREDIBLE: EVAL-101 protocol deviation — ran on wrong model, wrong n, skipped Cell C, no deviation doc; re-run required"
  status: done
  priority: P1
  effort: m
  description: |
    EVAL-101 closed as a null result (Δ=+0.025) but violated multiple RESEARCH_INTEGRITY.md
    requirements. The preregistration (docs/eval/preregistered/EVAL-101.md) specified:
    - Agent under test: claude-sonnet-4-20250514 (Anthropic API)
    - n per cell: 20 (underpowered; RESEARCH_INTEGRITY.md requires n≥50 for directional signal)
    - Cells: A/B/C (C skipped "due to Ollama timeout")
    - Judges: haiku + gpt-4o-mini (dual LLM)
    
    Actual run:
    - Agent: Qwen 2.5 14b (Ollama local) — different architecture, different base rates
    - n: 20 per cell (below the n≥50 floor in RESEARCH_INTEGRITY.md §1)
    - Cell C: omitted entirely (breaks confound control)
    - Judges: structural scoring only (no LLM judge despite being mandatory per RESEARCH_INTEGRITY.md §6)
    - Deviation section in preregistration: "(none yet)" — no deviation documentation
    - A/A baseline: not reported
    
    The preregistration's Deviations section still reads "(none yet)" despite all the above.
    The null result cannot be trusted as dispositive because the study ran on the wrong model.
    The cognition stack (reflections, lessons, neuromodulation) remains faith-based.
    
    Gap EVAL-101 was closed with `closed_date: '2026-05-10'` but has no cross_judge_audit
    or single_judge_waived fields — the INFRA-079 pre-commit guard should have blocked this.
  acceptance_criteria:
    - Deviations section in docs/eval/preregistered/EVAL-101.md updated with all deviations (model swap, n=20, Cell C skip, no LLM judge)
    - A new EVAL-* gap filed for the correct re-run (claude-sonnet-4, n≥50/cell, A/B/C, dual LLM judges)
    - EVAL-101 gap YAML updated with cross_judge_audit or single_judge_waived field to explain pre-commit bypass
