    Lane A: cargo check --workspace --all-targets --all-features on origin/main + every open PR head — find every other 'added field, missed initializer' / E0063 / dead-code class.
    
    Lane B: ci.yml lies — grep for 'rustup component add', 'cargo install', 'apt-get install', 'sccache --version' and dry-run each against the actual stable toolchain. Find every gate that depends on something that doesn't exist or doesn't work as-claimed.
    
    Lane C: trunk-RED detection latency. Trunk was RED for ~3h+ before we noticed. File trunk_red_detector daemon emits WARN on every red main run, bake into freshness-preamble + SessionStart hook.
    
    Lane D: preflight scope gaps. INFRA-2134 added a field to a shared struct but preflight scoped cargo check by diff (only same-crate) → missed. Fix: ANY Rust diff triggers cargo check --workspace, not just same-crate.
    
    Lane E: audit the 18+ wedged PRs once trunk green. Some may have latent issues hidden by cranelift fail-fast; demote ones that don't actually pass on their own merits.
    
    Dispatch pattern: 3 parallel Sonnets on A+B+D (independent); C blocks on D output; E blocks on trunk-green confirmation.
