- id: META-290
  domain: META
  title: "META UMBRELLA: plumbing-priority forcing function — fleet picks structural-wiring gaps at a guaranteed rate; idle umbrellas auto-decompose; CLAUDE.md doctrine-delta injection so agents see what just shipped"
  status: open
  priority: P2
  effort: l
  acceptance_criteria:
    - "docs/process/PLUMBING_PRIORITY.md exists: codifies the forcing function — when structural-PR-rate (% of last-N shipped PRs that closed gaps with effort=l OR title containing UMBRELLA/META/IGNITION/SUBSTRATE) drops below 25% rolling 14d, fleet pickability bias FLIPS toward plumbing for the next 7d."
    - "Sub-gaps decomposed and shipped: META-291 (umbrella-progress audit + decompose-cascade) + META-292 (SessionStart doctrine-delta injection)."
    - "CLAUDE.md gains a Plumbing-Priority section pointing to PLUMBING_PRIORITY.md + the rate metric. Picker doctrine: when in plumbing-bias mode, low-rated feature classes get demoted in tie-breaks."
    - "Empirical validation: after this umbrella ships, weekly structural_work_digest shows the rate above 25% for 4 consecutive weeks. Otherwise this umbrella did NOT solve the problem and stays open."
    - "Pillar-fit: this is META (forcing function for cross-cutting plumbing). Resists the trap that filed it as \"yet another feature gap that drowns in the queue\"."
  depends_on: [META-291, META-292]
  notes: |
    Origin: operator 2026-06-09T04:30Z "we never seem to get to this work". Inventory shows 20+ open umbrellas (MISSION-009 A2A, CREDIBLE-106 enforcement, EFFECTIVE-222 ignition, CREDIBLE-114 oxygen-hook, INFRA-2465 substrate-deprecation, META-033 invariants-cron, META-038 coord-tax, META-039 learning-loop, META-042 coord-cull, META-051 fix-one-wave) — most untouched for >7d while fleet ships 24 features/day. The gaps are not missing; the forcing function is missing. Closing this without changing the rate = not closed.
  opened_date: '2026-07-26'
  outcome_id: MISSION-010

- id: META-291
  domain: META
  title: umbrella-progress audit + decompose-cascade daemon — for every open effort=l umbrella, track days-since-last-PR-touching-its-files; >7d idle auto-files xs/s decomposition sub-gap; weekly structural-PR-rate digest emits kind=structural_work_digest; <25% structural-rate over 14d triggers operator-recall
  status: blocked
  priority: P2
  effort: s
  acceptance_criteria:
    - "scripts/coord/umbrella-progress-audit.sh runs every 6h (launchd plist dev.chump.umbrella-progress-audit). For each open gap matching effort=l AND (title contains UMBRELLA OR META OR IGNITION OR SUBSTRATE OR notes contains depends_on with effort=l gaps): grep AC for file paths/crate names; query git log to find last commit touching any matched path; record days-since-last-touch as kind=umbrella_progress_audit ambient event."
    - "When days-since-last-touch > 7 AND no sub-gaps filed (no other gap has this gap in depends_on): emit kind=umbrella_decompose_needed AND invoke chump gap decompose <ID> --dry-run, write the proposed decomposition to ~/.chump/proposed-decompositions/<ID>-<ts>.json. Operator reviews; non-operator agents can take from there."
    - "New CLI: chump health --structural-pr-rate [--window 14d] — computes % of last-N shipped PRs (where N defaults to last 14d) that closed gaps matching the plumbing pattern. Exits 1 if <25%. Used by META-290 plumbing-bias trigger."
    - "Weekly digest event: kind=structural_work_digest emitted Mondays 09:00 local, contains {open_umbrellas_count, avg_days_idle, structural_pr_rate_4w, oldest_untouched_umbrella_id, decompose_cascades_filed_last_week}."
    - "Operator-recall trigger: if structural_pr_rate_4w < 25% for 14 consecutive days, scripts/dispatch/operator-recall.sh fires with class=STRUCTURAL_STARVE."
    - "Test fixture: scripts/ci/test-umbrella-progress-audit.sh seeds 3 fake umbrella gaps with synthetic git history (one fresh, one 5d idle, one 30d idle); asserts only the 30d one triggers kind=umbrella_decompose_needed."
  notes: |
    Pairs with META-290 (umbrella). Without this audit, "we never get to this work" recurs every cycle. The decompose-cascade is the unblock — turns L into xs/s slices the picker actually pulls.
    
    [2026-08-28T18:09:54Z] INFRA-3832 auto-block: 3 consecutive non-ship cycles (last kind=rc=143, rc=143, cycle_log=0B). Worker kept re-picking + looping; blocked to leave the pick pool. Un-block after fixing the spec / decomposing.
  opened_date: '2026-07-26'
  outcome_id: MISSION-010

- id: META-292
  domain: META
  title: SessionStart doctrine-delta injection — surface 'CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md/docs/process/* changes since session's last commit' in the digest, so agents see what doctrine just shipped (today CREDIBLE-105 shipped during my session; tomorrow's agent has no reason to know unless they re-read the whole file)
  status: blocked
  priority: P2
  effort: s
  acceptance_criteria:
    - scripts/coord/doctrine-delta-inject.sh wired into SessionStart hook (alongside ambient-context-inject.sh + inbox-check-urgent.sh).
    - "On SessionStart: read ~/.chump/session-last-doctrine-commit (file storing last-seen origin/main commit for doctrine paths); run git log <stored-commit>..origin/main --name-only -- CLAUDE.md AGENTS.md docs/process/*.md docs/MISSION.md to enumerate doctrine changes; format as \"Doctrine changes since your last session\" block in the session digest."
    - "Operator-directive freshness sub-check: when SessionStart context contains an operator directive with file-path + line-number references (e.g. \"fix line 2927 in src/main.rs\"), verify the file exists at origin/main HEAD and emit a \"directive freshness\" line: \"✓ verified at HEAD\" or \"⚠ src/main.rs has been modified since this directive — line numbers may have shifted N lines\"."
    - Update ~/.chump/session-last-doctrine-commit on each session START with current origin/main HEAD (not on session end — session end may not fire on crash).
    - "Smoke test scripts/ci/test-doctrine-delta-inject.sh: seed a fake last-doctrine-commit pointing at 2 commits ago; run inject; assert digest contains the 2 doctrine commits in human-readable form."
  notes: |
    Origin: operator 2026-06-09 framing #8 "doctrine ships faster than CLAUDE.md updates". Real example: CREDIBLE-105 (no-band-aids) was filed AND shipped during my Jun 5 session. Jun 6 agents had no copy; Jun 7 agents only saw it because I had MEMORY.md context. Without this, every doctrine change has a multi-day visibility lag. Paired with META-290 + META-291 to close the discoverability cliff named in operator framing #3.
    
    [2026-08-28T17:44:09Z] INFRA-3832 auto-block: 3 consecutive non-ship cycles (last kind=rc=143, rc=143, cycle_log=12288B). Worker kept re-picking + looping; blocked to leave the pick pool. Un-block after fixing the spec / decomposing.
