- id: META-328
  domain: META
  title: "META: outcome-table drift + one weekly verdict — compose mission-grade, roadmap-status and the scoreboard into counsel"
  status: open
  priority: P2
  effort: s
  description: |
    RE-SCOPED 2026-08-07 after the operator asked whether prior art existed and it did. Title rewritten under CHUMP_ALLOW_GAP_REWRITE (INFRA-456's sanctioned correction path) because the original — 'the fleet has no conscience' — is factually FALSE: partial conscience machinery exists and runs. ORIGINAL SCOPE WAS WRONG. What exists, mine it rather than rebuild: (1) 'chump mission-grade' (INFRA-599) computes per-pillar pickable/in-flight/shipped-24h every 30 min via launchd, emitting a kind=mission_grade ambient event; (2) 'chump roadmap-status' (INFRA-606, INFRA-1145) parses docs/ROADMAP.md weekly outcomes against state.db and ALREADY implements starved_outcomes, untraced_p0, pillar_coverage and --exit-on-drift — verified by running it 2026-08-07: it printed Weeks 1-4, 'No starved outcomes', 3 untraced P1s, and pillar coverage; (3) scripts/dev/mission-scoreboard.sh reports the four mission gates including the mission-ship ratio against its 2/3 scaling gate (15/28 on 2026-08-07, up from 5/18 two days earlier); (4) INFRA-3499 (~50% built) is the do->reflect loop with the hook already WIRED at autonomy_loop.rs:1352 — per-work-item reflection, adjacent to but distinct from periodic fleet coherence. WHAT IS ACTUALLY MISSING and all this gap now builds: (a) roadmap-status drift covers ROADMAP.md's WEEKLY outcomes, NOT the outcome table — which is why it truthfully printed 'No starved outcomes' on a day when LIGHTHOUSE-OLIVE and LIGHTHOUSE-UPSHIFT held zero gaps and LIGHTHOUSE-ARCADE held one, against MISSION-010's 2,621; (b) nothing composes these four sources into ONE verdict, so a whole-system drift required a human pass to surface; (c) the registry cannot distinguish a DELIBERATELY PARKED outcome from a neglected one — the ambiguity that made a considered factory-first sequencing read as drift.
  acceptance_criteria:
    - the drift analysis in roadmap-status is EXTENDED to cover the outcome table (outcomes with a stated DoD and zero open gaps; outcomes whose children are all unpickable) — extend that command, never add a parallel checker
    - the registry supports marking an outcome deliberately parked WITH a reason, and a parked outcome reports as parked rather than starved — the LIGHTHOUSE outcomes on 2026-08-07 are the test case
    - "one weekly composition reads mission-grade, roadmap-status, mission-scoreboard and the factory matrix and emits a SINGLE operator-readable verdict: at most three things worth changing, each naming which organ produced it"
    - every line traces to a mechanical check from those existing sources — the model synthesizes and prioritizes, it never detects (judgment-panel architecture, CREDIBLE-191)
    - "the verdict can be APPROVAL: a run where nothing drifts says so and stops, and that outcome is reachable by construction"
    - delivered where the operator already looks (FLEET-RADIO), weekly not hourly — reflection, not monitoring
    - "dogfood receipt: the first run reproduces the outcome-table finding a human made on 2026-08-07 (three product lighthouses at 0/0/1 against MISSION-010's 2,621); if it cannot, it is not measuring the right thing"
  depends_on: [INFRA-3499]
  notes: |
    Over-scoped on first filing because I skipped the DOC-082 dedupe check — I specified mechanical checks that already ship and run every 30 minutes. Third such miss this session: CREDIBLE-217 superseded into EFFECTIVE-389 for the same reason, and EFFECTIVE-383 was saved only because EFFECTIVE-386 happened to ship mid-session. Caught by the operator asking 'did you look first'. Effort m->s: composition plus one extension, not a build.
  opened_date: '2026-08-19'
  outcome_id: CHUMPOS

- id: META-329
  domain: META
  title: "META: add R&D as the fifth pillar — 37 files enumerate the four-pillar set"
  status: open
  priority: P3
  effort: m
  description: |
    Operator decision 2026-08-08: fifth pillar, not a separate ledger. Design and reasoning in docs/rfcs/RFC-rnd-pillar.md (shipped PR #3526, corrected #3530). Mechanical but broad: 37 files enumerate EFFECTIVE|CREDIBLE|RESILIENT|ZERO-WASTE, including mission_grade.rs (classifies by gap-title prefix, case-insensitive, untagged excluded), roadmap_status.rs (pillar_coverage), kpi_report.rs, health.rs, execute_gap.rs, fleet_health.rs, intent_parser.rs, completion.rs. Chose pillar over ledger specifically to inherit the curator's balance_restock, which is the only thing that prevents silent starvation — so this gap is only worth landing if RESILIENT-246 revives the curator, otherwise the fifth pillar starves on day one exactly like the LIGHTHOUSE outcomes. R&D's success axis inverts (learning per spend; a fast NO-GO is a win), so it must not be summed into pillar metrics built for delivered value. Ship-ratio exclusion is a SEPARATE gap because forgetting it corrupts the scaling gate.
  acceptance_criteria:
    - "R&D: is a recognized gap-title prefix everywhere the other four are — enumerated, not special-cased, so the next pillar is a one-line change"
    - chump gap reserve --domain R&D works and mission_grade counts it in pillar inventory
    - pillar_coverage in roadmap-status reports R&D alongside the others
    - "a gap titled 'R&D: ...' is pickable and shippable end to end, proven by one real trivial R&D gap through the pipeline"
    - R&D's inverted success axis is documented where mission_grade computes pillar health, so nobody later sums learning-per-spend into delivered-value metrics
    - "blocked until RESILIENT-246 restores the curator: without balance_restock a fifth pillar starves silently"
  depends_on: [RESILIENT-246]
  opened_date: '2026-08-19'
  outcome_id: CHUMPOS

- id: META-330
  domain: META
  title: "META: backfill the six NO-GOs as R&D's founding history so the pillar does not launch at 0%"
  status: open
  priority: P2
  effort: s
  description: |
    A new pillar at zero reads as neglect, which is precisely the trap the three LIGHTHOUSE outcomes are sitting in (0, 0 and 1 gaps against MISSION-010's 2,621 — a goal with no work looks like a wish). R&D does not need to launch empty: six go/no-go verdicts already exist and are currently filed as FAILURES. Under the pillar they are the product — a fast NO-GO is a successful run. The best-documented is the posse-outward bet: venture-go-no-go workflow, 7 agents, survived 0 of 3 kill attempts, killed on economics not technology, accepted by the operator 2026-08-04, and the reasoning preserved in posse/OUTWARD_READINESS.md. Backfill each as an R&D gap with its verdict, what it cost, and what was learned — retro-tagged, not re-litigated. Also worth capturing: the embedder A/B that came back a wash, and the cross-encoder rerank measured negative and left OFF, both of which are real R&D returns the fleet already banked.
  acceptance_criteria:
    - each of the six NO-GOs exists as a closed R&D gap carrying its verdict, spend if known, and what was learned — with a pointer to where the reasoning already lives rather than a rewrite
    - the pillar shows non-zero history on its first day, so a coherence check (META-328) reads it as deliberate rather than starving
    - a NO-GO is recorded as a SUCCESSFUL outcome, not a failure — if the registry cannot express that, say so rather than filing them as losses
    - "the embedder A/B (a wash) and the rerank measurement (negative, left off) are included: a null result is the pillar's product"
    - no verdict is re-opened or re-argued; this is bookkeeping
  depends_on: [META-329]
  opened_date: '2026-08-19'

- id: META-331
  domain: META
  title: "RESILIENT: node contract — declare, verify, and enforce fleet node substrate"
  status: open
  priority: P2
  effort: m
  description: |
    Written the night of the 2026-08-09 closetjunky recovery. The fleet coordinates WORK well (gaps, leases, NATS, consensus) and does not model SUBSTRATE at all: no node identity, no registry, no security baseline, no boot-persistence verification, no storage inventory, no node-level liveness. Seven of the nine lifecycle phases failed in a single evening. Sub-gaps DOC-098 (Wi-Fi bringup runbook) and RESILIENT-282 (baseline enforcement) are already filed.
  acceptance_criteria:
    - "docs/design/FLEET_NODE_ARCHITECTURE.md lands: the node contract (declare + verify), nine lifecycle phases, the node record schema, an honest claimed-vs-verified table, and a four-wave plan"
    - "Wave 1 declares: node identity generator writing ~/.chump/node-id.txt, an in-repo registry at docs/fleet/nodes/<node-id>.yaml holding posture facts only and never credentials, and chump node contract show"
    - verify
    - META-128 C2 (chump-disk-inventory daemon) is folded in as the first inventory producer rather than re-filed; today chump disk status
    - plan
    - budget ship while the daemon and ~/.chump/disk-inventory.json do not exist on any node
    - "Wave 2 enforces: a node failing the security baseline is REFUSED WORK by the picker, not merely flagged (operator decision 2026-08-09)"
    - Every node is in scope including the Mac (operator decision 2026-08-09)
    - "Verification cadence is aggressive: on-change plus a short periodic floor, per operator decision 2026-08-09 to be as aggressive as needed to keep things running"
    - Node liveness is tracked independently of fleet ship-rate, because closetjunky was offline 5 days while the fleet shipped from other nodes and nothing paged
  opened_date: '2026-08-19'
  outcome_id: MISSION-010

