  title: "MISSION: chumpd state-API socket — CLI asks the daemon for the canonical db path instead of guessing from cwd (kills resolve-by-cwd class at the root; MISSION-051 slice 2)"
  status: done
  priority: P1
  effort: m
  description: |
    Ground-up step 2, slice 2 (docs/design/GROUND_UP_2026-07-19.md): chumpd owns a unix socket (~/.chump/chumpd.sock) answering read-only queries: ping, status (the status JSON), db-path (canonical .chump/state.db path from chumpd's CHUMP_REPO). The chump CLI's db resolution tries the socket FIRST (50ms budget) and falls back to today's cwd-walk when the socket is absent — so every chump gap set/show/reserve from ANY worktree resolves canonical automatically. This deletes the disease behind CREDIBLE-154's phantom ships, INFRA-3338's ID collisions, and the INFRA-3340/3341 false pillar-starved alarms.
