- id: MISSION-076
  domain: MISSION
  title: "multi-repo execution lane: ChumpOS can TAG external-repo work but cannot EXECUTE it — 77 gaps stranded"
  status: blocked
  priority: P2
  effort: l
  acceptance_criteria:
    - "STATE (verified 2026-08-07): external_repo:<owner>/<repo> is consumed ONLY as a derived index (chump-gap-store lib.rs:4488 upserts a repos row per tag). Neither dispatch.rs nor execute_gap.rs mentions it. So a worker claiming one of the 77 open external-repo gaps gets a CHUMP worktree, grounded against CHUMP's almanac index (EFFECTIVE-390), gated by cargo test + chump's hooks, shipped by bot-merge into CHUMP's main — for work that lives in olive, slidemate or ai-gm-service. This is not serialization, it is a missing execution path"
    - "SEPARATE THE BOUNDARY: kernel = gap registry, claim/lease, dispatch, almanac (already per-repo), holler. Userland = checkout, test cmd, lint/build, CI, ship pipeline, merge policy. Today Chump's userland is wrongly assumed universal — bot-merge's gates, the cargo-test pre-push gate and the main.rs merge driver are all Chump-specific"
    - "CRAWL (do first): read-only. Organs+almanac sweep N repos, file findings to holler, zero writes to any repo. Already specified as EFFECTIVE-398 (organs emit --findings-json) -> EFFECTIVE-389 (scheduled sweep). Crawl also PRODUCES the backlog walk consumes, so it is a dependency not just caution"
    - "WALK: dispatch clones/worktrees the TARGET repo, agent works there, opens a PR against THAT repo, and THAT repo's own CI is the gate. Chump's gates must not apply. Needs the missing primitive: a per-repo contract (how to test, how to ship). DERIVE it by default rather than author it — measured: olive test='npm run lint && npm run build', upshift test='npm run e2e:all'; holler/posse genuinely have none, which is a valid answer not a failure. Hang it off the existing repos table, which already carries last_clone_at and last_ship_at columns that anticipate exactly this"
    - "RUN: many repos concurrently + autonomous merge. Gate on proven walk, a per-repo merge policy (which repos may auto-merge vs require a human), and a GLOBAL governor — the real parallelism limits are machine resources (145 live worktrees today; ~60-94 ptys per Agent-tool dispatch per SUBAGENT_DISPATCH), GitHub API rate (there is already a gh-throttle window + _chump_gh_classify_call), and inference capacity (Ollama contention observed 2026-08-06). NOT merge conflicts"
    - "WHY CROSS-REPO IS SAFER THAN TODAY: every collision hit on 2026-08-06/07 was WITHIN chump — main.rs +6081/-6089 conflict (PR #3499), a shared dirty checkout between sibling sessions, a DEPTH.md test-count race, an ALMANAC_HOME env race. Different repos touch different files; fanning out REDUCES contention on the one hot repo"
    - "OBSERVATION BEFORE ACTION: do not run autonomous agents across 90 repos while CREDIBLE-220 (nothing watches non-chump CI — two repos sat red ~6 months) and RESILIENT-247 (pr-rescue.sh exists but is unscheduled) are open. You cannot supervise what you cannot see"
  notes: |
    Decomposed into 6 slices: MISSION-097, MISSION-098, MISSION-099, MISSION-100, MISSION-101, MISSION-102
    [2026-09-10T12:00:32Z] INFRA-3832 auto-block: 3 consecutive non-ship cycles (last kind=rc=1, rc=1, cycle_log=2875B). Worker kept re-picking + looping; blocked to leave the pick pool. Un-block after fixing the spec / decomposing.
  opened_date: '2026-08-19'
  outcome_id: MISSION-032

- id: MISSION-077
  domain: MISSION
  title: picker scores score(gap) not score(gap, agent) — fine for one repo, wrong the moment agents differ
  status: blocked
  priority: P2
  effort: l
  acceptance_criteria:
    - "STATE (verified 2026-08-07): chump-planner/src/score.rs weighs priority, effort, unblocking_bonus, cycle_age, roadmap_alignment — all properties of the GAP. score() never takes an agent. That is correct while every worker is interchangeable (Claude, one repo, warm context) and becomes wrong the moment agents differ by repo, language or capability"
    - "DEAD ROUTING SCHEMA: gaps already carry skills_required, preferred_backend, preferred_machine, required_model, estimated_minutes (INFRA-314, INFRA-418). Of 233 open gaps: 0 populate backend, machine, model or estimated_minutes, and the 77 non-empty skills_required are all just the external_repo tag, not skills. Nothing in the planner or autonomy loop reads any of them. Either populate and use them, or delete them — a schema that lies about its own capability is worse than an honest gap"
    - "REPO AFFINITY is the load-bearing addition for multi-repo, and it is an economics argument not a preference: per-repo cold start is real (clone+index of a mid-size repo runs minutes; almanac reindex of chump alone is 21.8s). A picker with no locality makes an agent pay clone+index on every pick. An agent that just worked olive should strongly prefer the next olive gap — CPU-cache-affinity semantics, or a repo lease drained before switching"
    - "CAPABILITY MATCH, using prior art already inventoried in opportunity-library/ROUTING_SYSTEMS.md rather than invented: beast-mode's a2a_agents (capabilities TEXT[] + GIN index + load + last_seen, with 5-min staleness eviction) is the strongest matcher in the fleet; SpecialistRouter's learned tiebreak successRate*(1+log10(evidence+1)) with a >0.7 override gate is the bandit-lite layer; jarvis farm-balancer's busy<parallel capacity gate is the backpressure model"
    - "INTERNAL vs EXTERNAL agents resolve to the SAME mechanism once score takes an agent: an internal tmux worker and an external service (a Copilot-style cloud agent on another repo) are both just agents with different capability sets, load and locality. Do not build two pickers"
    - "SEQUENCING: this is a WALK-stage dependency of MISSION-076, not a crawl-stage one. Crawl is read-only and needs no capability routing. Do not build this before crawl produces the multi-repo backlog it is meant to route"
  notes: |
    [2026-08-08T02:17:09Z] PREMISE CORRECTION 2026-08-07 — this is WIRING, not building. Both halves already exist and neither is called.
    
    WORKER SIDE, twice over:
    - crates/chump-coord/src/worker/capability.rs:69 WorkerCapability { skills (from WORKER_SKILLS env), machine (WORKER_MACHINE), backend (WORKER_BACKEND), session_id }. Its own module doc at worker/mod.rs:10 calls it a 'picker filter', and it is designed to match gaps.preferred_machine / preferred_backend.
    - crates/chump-team/src/capabilities.rs:36 WorkerCapability { team_id, user_id, machine, skills: Vec<String>, backend (Claude|Opencode|Codex|Manual), max_concurrent_gaps, last_heartbeat_at }. Postgrest/Supabase-backed. This is capability match + capacity gate + liveness heartbeat — precisely the a2a_agents + jarvis-farm-balancer combination ROUTING_SYSTEMS.md recommends grafting, already implemented in-house.
    
    GAP SIDE: gaps carry skills_required, preferred_backend, preferred_machine, required_model, estimated_minutes.
    
    THE WIRE IS MISSING ON BOTH ENDS: 0 of 233 open gaps populate backend/machine/model/estimated_minutes, and neither chump-planner nor autonomy_loop.rs ever constructs or consults a WorkerCapability. Grep confirms the coord picker-filter has zero callers outside its own crate.
    
    CONSEQUENCE FOR EFFORT: likely smaller than the 'l' this was filed at — closer to connecting two finished halves plus a backfill of the gap-side fields, than to designing capability routing.
    
    CONSEQUENCE FOR PRODUCT TEAMS (operator question, same day): teams are ALREADY the data model — chump-team carries team_id and OperatorQuota. And a worker can ALREADY declare a specialty at launch via WORKER_SKILLS / WORKER_MACHINE / WORKER_BACKEND. What is missing is only the honoring: nothing reads the declaration when picking. So 'product team per repo' is a launch-flag + picker-filter change, not new architecture.
    
    This is the fifth instance today of the same fleet pattern: instrument built, never run (cf. pr-rescue.sh unscheduled RESILIENT-247, non-chump CI unwatched CREDIBLE-220, organs never swept EFFECTIVE-389, tracemap never pointed at its own example input EFFECTIVE-397).
    [2026-09-10T12:30:25Z] INFRA-3832 auto-block: 3 consecutive non-ship cycles (last kind=rc=1, rc=1, cycle_log=4206B). Worker kept re-picking + looping; blocked to leave the pick pool. Un-block after fixing the spec / decomposing.
  opened_date: '2026-08-19'
  outcome_id: MISSION-032

