- id: PRODUCT-141
  domain: PRODUCT
  title: "chump assess <repo>: check-then-generate roadmap + generalized % to goal, not tool-specific format"
  status: open
  priority: P2
  effort: l
  description: |
    The end goal of today's whole thread (INFRA-3526/3527/3529/3530/3531): a human should be able to ask Chump 'how baked is repo X' and get a real, computed % against a real, current goal — not a first-mate session spending an entire evening manually reading files by hand, which is what actually happened 2026-08-02 and which does not scale past a handful of repos.
    
    What exists today, all pieces, none connected:
    - roadmap TRACKER: chump roadmap-status parses docs/ROADMAP.md into milestone %, but ONLY Chump's own weekly-outcome format. Olive's roadmap is a status-tagged ticket-table (EX/LI/BR/P0 tracks, checkbox status per ticket). Upshift's is a 1300-line phase narrative. grave-dancer's is a phased build doc with prose 'Done when' criteria per phase. Four real formats found in one afternoon; roadmap-status understands exactly one of them.
    - roadmap WRITER: RoadmapFromVisionContract (chump-handoff), a real typed LLM contract, zero callers anywhere (INFRA-3527, still open).
    - doc VISIBILITY: FIXED today (INFRA-3531) — markdown finally reaches almanac's index, so a check-first step can actually find an existing roadmap instead of assuming none exists.
    
    The specific mistake this gap exists to prevent, made twice today before being caught: almanac's markdown blindness (now fixed) led to confidently concluding olive and upshift-platform had NO defined goal, when both had real, current, substantial roadmaps sitting in docs/. Generating a NEW roadmap for a repo that already has one — without checking first — is exactly how BEAST-MODE ended up with 127 competing, all-abandoned planning documents (found 2026-08-02, zero of them touched in 30 days). Absence-of-plan and abundance-of-abandoned-plans are the same failure mode: nobody checked before writing.
    
    Scope: a 'chump assess <repo>' command/workflow that (1) checks for an existing roadmap/plan doc via almanac search first — now that markdown is visible, this is finally possible; (2) if found, parses it into a generalized status model (done/in-progress/not-started per item, regardless of the four+ formats already found in this portfolio alone) rather than assuming Chump's own ROADMAP.md shape; (3) if genuinely absent, offers to generate one via RoadmapFromVisionContract (INFRA-3527) rather than silently proceeding without one; (4) computes and reports a real % against whatever goal the roadmap states, with the same honesty discipline this session used by hand — a % is only reported when a real goal exists, never invented against an assumed one.
  acceptance_criteria:
    - checks for an existing plan doc (via almanac, post-INFRA-3531) before ever proposing to generate one
    - correctly parses at least the 3 real formats found this session (Chump's own weekly-outcome ROADMAP.md, a status-tagged ticket-table like olive's, a phased prose doc like grave-dancer's/upshift's) into one common done/in-progress/not-started model
    - refuses to compute a % when no real goal exists, and says so explicitly rather than defaulting to a health-score substitute (the exact mistake corrected mid-session in PORTFOLIO_READINESS.md)
    - if it finds an abandoned-plan-pile situation (multiple stale competing docs, BEAST-MODE-style) it flags that explicitly rather than picking one arbitrarily and pretending it's canonical
    - tested against at least 2 real repos in this portfolio with different roadmap formats, not just synthetic fixtures
  depends_on: [INFRA-3527]
  source_doc: session 2026-08-02, the full roadmap/%-to-goal investigation
  opened_date: '2026-08-19'
  outcome_id: META-067

- id: PRODUCT-142
  domain: PRODUCT
  title: "feedback-triage: judge holler inbox rows before gap creation (valid/noise/needs-human/harmful)"
  status: blocked
  priority: P2
  effort: m
  description: |
    holler (github.com/repairman29/holler) is a portfolio-wide feedback substrate now scaling beyond the games workspace to real product pages (olive live as of today) ahead of public posting (Facebook). Its own bot->holler->chump bridge (games/shared/playtest/holler-to-chump.mjs, precedent: GAME-001..005) works today but was built for BOT-GENERATED findings, which are inherently trustworthy (deterministic output of test/probe code -- 'SPAWN_IN_COLLISION on X' cannot be spam, wrong, or hostile). Real human free-text input from a public audience does not have that property and needs a judgment step the bot pipeline never required. This is architecturally a PUSH pattern, distinct from chump's existing PULL-based gap discovery (an agent going out to find work): the finding already arrived (a stranger typed something into a box); the job is validating and translating an already-arrived signal, not discovering a new one. Holler's job stays infra-only: collect, rate-limit, dedupe-by-hash, expose feedback_inbox (hides handled rows, counts hits per dedupe_hash) and inbox.mjs --new (schedulable, only-what's-new-since-last-check). This gap is the chump-side judge that sits between 'row lands in holler' and 'gap gets filed.' No holler schema change is needed: context is already free-form jsonb and feedback_inbox already filters on context->>'status', so the judge just needs to write back e.g. {"status": "triaged", "verdict": "..."} using the service role key (same key inbox.mjs already uses) to mark a row processed.
  acceptance_criteria:
    - "Output is a 4-way classification per row, not a binary valid/invalid: (1) actionable = real bug/idea worth a gap; (2) noise = spam, test junk, gibberish, low-content praise; (3) needs-human = genuinely ambiguous or high-stakes enough that silent auto-filing is wrong; (4) harmful = content requiring escalation (e.g. abuse/threats) -- kept as its own axis, never conflated with noise or with harshly-worded-but-legitimate criticism, which must classify as actionable or needs-human, not harmful, just for being negative"
    - Before filing a NEW gap for an actionable row, checks chump's OWN gap registry for an existing open gap on the same underlying issue using real semantic similarity (not just holler's dedupe_hash, which only catches identical client-side error callsites) -- reuse/call into existing gap triage / gap consolidate tooling (INFRA-935) rather than reinventing dedup
    - Uses chump's provider-agnostic LLM cascade (ProviderCascade / chump-local default per Principle 0), never a hardcoded single vendor
    - Every processed row gets context->>'status' written back via the service role key so feedback_inbox naturally excludes it from the next pass -- no new holler schema/column required, verify this against the live view before assuming
    - needs-human and harmful verdicts have a real escalation path (e.g. a flagged-for-review gap list or notification), never silently auto-filed as a normal gap and never silently dropped
    - Extends the existing holler-to-chump.mjs bridge mechanics (idempotent local ledger, external_repo tagging generalized per-project e.g. repairman29/olive) rather than a parallel implementation
    - Ships with real test cases across all 4 verdict axes including at least one adversarial harmful-content case and one harshly-worded-but-legitimate case, verified against real (not synthetic-only) holler rows before merge
    - False-negative risk on the harmful axis is explicitly documented (what this catches vs. what it doesn't), not silently assumed complete
  notes: |
    Filed 2026-08-02 from a first-mate session scaling holler to olive + designing this feed at the operator's explicit direction: 'it's a chump thing not a holler thing... I think chump can actually do the spiritual heavy lifting of is this feedback even valid.' Higher scrutiny than typical P2 work given the harm-axis false-negative stakes -- do not treat this as routine triage tooling.
    [2026-09-03T18:25:14Z] INFRA-3832 auto-block: 3 consecutive non-ship cycles (last kind=timeout, rc=124, cycle_log=3924581B). Worker kept re-picking + looping; blocked to leave the pick pool. Un-block after fixing the spec / decomposing.
  opened_date: '2026-08-19'

