- id: PRODUCT-169
  domain: PRODUCT
  title: "[chump] Rust builds duplicated: crons on stable(1.97.1) vs sessions pinned 1.96.0, plus split CARGO_TARGET_DIRs"
  status: done
  priority: P2
  effort: s
  description: |
    Storage survey 2026-08-04, receipts live. (1) chump-binary-refresh cron builds with the stable toolchain (1.97.1) while interactive sessions pin 1.96.0 - every crate compiles twice into every cache. (2) The refresh cron uses CARGO_TARGET_DIR=~/Projects/Chump/target while sessions use ~/.cargo/chump-shared-target - zero artifact sharing between them. (3) Chump/target was recently zeroed, so the cron cold-builds all of Chump every run (observed live: 4+ min release build from a /tmp clone). The shared cache had bloated to ~70GB of orphaned layers; cargo-sweep -t30 reclaimed 36GiB on 2026-08-04. Fix: ONE pinned toolchain via rust-toolchain.toml in repo root + ONE shared CARGO_TARGET_DIR for sessions and crons. DECISION IS THE CAPTAIN'S (parked in ~/Projects/TODO.md 2026-08-04) - implement only after blessing. Follow-up hygiene: a monthly cargo-sweep cron keeps the cache from re-bloating.
    
