- id: PRODUCT-170
  domain: PRODUCT
  title: "[chump] task_list silently widens unknown status filters to all-active (e2e queried ?status=pending green for months)"
  status: blocked
  priority: P2
  effort: s
  description: |
    Found by the e2e depth pass (chump#3453, merged 2026-08-02). src/task_db.rs:194: task_list matches known statuses (open|blocked|in_progress|done|abandoned) and treats ANY unknown filter as "all active". The e2e suite queried ?status=pending - not a real status - and stayed green because the assert only checked non-emptiness. The test now pins real behavior (created row asserted by id in the open list), but the API design question is open: should handle_tasks_list 400 on unknown status values instead of silently widening? Silent widening means a typo in any caller returns everything and no one notices.
    
