- id: RESILIENT-049
  domain: RESILIENT
  title: "audit + ban Stdio::null() on git/external commands — silent failures hide test regressions"
  status: blocked
  priority: P2
  effort: s
  description: |
    tokio::process::Command::....stderr(Stdio::null())....status() silently swallows command failures. This blocks the surrounding code from learning about (or asserting on) git/external-binary errors.
    
    Discovered 2026-05-30 during PR #2866 trunk-RED diagnosis: chump-integrator's test helper init_repo_with_commits() called git init then git checkout main, both with .stderr(Stdio::null()). On CI runners with init.defaultBranch=master, git init created a 'master' branch; the subsequent 'git checkout main' silently failed; branch B was then created off branch A instead of off main; the test's expected conflict didn't happen; test failed in a way that took human debugging to root-cause (4+ months later, when it finally surfaced).
    
    Anti-pattern: Stdio::null() should never be used for STDERR of error-checked commands. If we want to suppress noise, use a buffered Stdio::piped() and only print on failure.
    
    PROPOSAL:
    1. Scan crates/**/*.rs for .stderr(Stdio::null()) preceded by a Command. Audit each: is the exit code checked? Is failure-mode reachable?
    2. For each unchecked-stderr-and-status case: refactor to capture stderr to a buffer; on non-zero exit, propagate it.
    3. Add clippy lint or custom check (regex over .rs files in CI) that flags this combination.
    4. Document the rule in docs/process/CODE_REVIEW.md or similar.
    
    This is the 'silent agent' class — fail without surfacing what failed. Already known via other paths (silent_agent ambient event) but this is the source-code instance.
  acceptance_criteria:
    - "TODO: what events emitted on success/failure/timeout"
    - "TODO: how cost tracked and reported to operator"
    - "TODO: failure-class taxonomy (distinguish transient vs permanent)"
    - "TODO: smoke test command to verify observability"
  notes: |
    [2026-08-29T11:42:25Z] INFRA-3832 auto-block: 3 consecutive non-ship cycles (last kind=rc=1, rc=1, cycle_log=6004B). Worker kept re-picking + looping; blocked to leave the pick pool. Un-block after fixing the spec / decomposing.
  opened_date: '2026-07-26'
  outcome_id: RESILIENT-000

- id: RESILIENT-050
  domain: RESILIENT
  title: "P0: stale-pr-reaper MUST hold during trunk-RED — destroyed 28 legitimate PRs at 2026-05-30T15:46Z"
  status: done
  priority: P1
  effort: s
  description: |
    INCIDENT 2026-05-30T15:45-15:46Z: scripts/ops/stale-pr-reaper.sh (INFRA-1410 SLO enforcer) auto-closed 28 in-flight PRs in 60 seconds because they were BLOCKED for >2h30m. The PRs were BLOCKED because TRUNK WAS RED — every PR's required checks (cargo-test, coverage) were failing on a known root cause (chump-integrator test_conflict_aborts_with_structured_error regression). Hotfix PR #2866 was in CI; once it lands, all 28 would have cascade-merged.
    
    Instead, the reaper destroyed all 28. Operator caught it, daemon was force-unloaded, all 28 PRs reopened + auto-merge re-armed at 2026-05-30T15:51Z. Time-cost of incident: ~10 min operator + ~5 min recovery automation.
    
    ROOT CAUSE: stale-pr-reaper does not check trunk-RED state before bouncing. INFRA-1410 SLO is meant to flush PRs stuck on their OWN merits (not the queue-wide blocker class).
    
    FIX: stale-pr-reaper.sh must, before bouncing any PR:
      1. Check trunk-RED state (latest run on main, conclusion==failure for cargo-test or similar required-check class)
      2. If trunk-RED → emit kind=reaper_holding_for_trunk_red to ambient + skip ALL bounces this cycle (do NOT close PRs whose BLOCKED state is downstream of trunk-RED, not their own bug)
      3. If trunk-GREEN but THIS PR has a unique failure (not the same as 5+ other PRs) → proceed with bounce
      4. Add config flag CHUMP_REAPER_HOLD_TRUNK_RED (default ON) for emergency override
    
    Coordination: trunk-red-detector daemon (META-177 Lane C, in PR #2863 — ALSO reaped, now reopened) ships the trunk-RED state file at .chump-locks/trunk-red-detector-state.json. Reaper reads that file.
    
    URGENCY: P0. Daemon currently disabled via launchctl unload. Must ship the trunk-RED gate before re-enabling, OR keep reaper disabled until fix lands.
  acceptance_criteria:
    - stale-pr-reaper.sh checks trunk-RED state before bouncing; emits reaper_holding_for_trunk_red when trunk is RED; test passes
  closed_date: '2026-06-05'
  closed_pr: 2867
  outcome_id: RESILIENT-000

