- id: RESILIENT-052
  domain: RESILIENT
  title: "bot-merge exit-144-silent recurs post-#2169 — root-cause + loud-fail + regression test"
  status: done
  priority: P1
  effort: m
  acceptance_criteria:
    - bot-merge no longer exits 144 silently; on failure it prints the failing step and a non-zero diagnosable cause, and a regression test reproduces the exit-144 condition asserting a loud failure.
  notes: |
    RECONCILE (2nd pass): already shipped via PR #4010 (8cb1bcb6, "fix(RESILIENT-052):
    bot-merge ERR trap — root-cause + loud-fail for silent exit-144"). First reconcile
    (PR #4016) correctly set status:done/closed_pr:4010, but the bulk-reconcile commit
    548b96ed (PR #4018, "BULK reconcile state.db→yaml in one pass") clobbered it back
    to status:open by reading a stale/empty state.db snapshot that didn't have this
    gap's done row — regressing an already-closed gap. Filed INFRA follow-up for the
    bulk-reconcile script to skip/warn on gaps whose YAML already carries closed_pr
    rather than blindly overwriting from a possibly-stale db read.
    
    Root cause (INFRA-2688): bot-merge.sh ran under `set -euo pipefail` with
    no ERR trap, so any child process dying non-zero (e.g. a gh sub-process
    killed by SIGURG, exit 128+16=144) propagated silently — indistinguishable
    from a hang. Fix adds `trap '_bm_err_handler "$?" "$BASH_COMMAND" "$LINENO"' ERR`
    (scripts/coord/bot-merge.sh:396) which prints the failing step, exit code,
    and decoded signal name to stderr and emits kind=bot_merge_uncaught_error
    to ambient.jsonl (registered in EVENT_REGISTRY.yaml).
    scripts/ci/test-bot-merge-err-trap-loud-fail.sh reproduces the exit-144
    condition against the real extracted handler and asserts a loud
    diagnosable failure + ambient event — 10/10 assertions pass. All AC
    bullets are met.
  closed_date: '2026-08-20'
  closed_pr: 4010
  outcome_id: RESILIENT-000

