  description: |
    VERIFIED 2026-06-05 17:33Z (musher session, post-MISSION-033 #3073 deploy attempt). MISSION-012 auto-deploy daemon (com.chump.auto-deploy) invokes scripts/ops/refresh-runner-binary.sh which creates a worktree at /tmp/chump-binary-refresh-<PID>/ then runs 'cargo build --release --bin chump' in it. Build takes 10-12 min. PROBLEM: /tmp/chump-binary-refresh-* matches the pattern stale-worktree-reaper.sh + active-target-reaper.sh scan (any /tmp/chump-*/). Mid-build, the reaper deletes the worktree's target/release/deps/ which causes: 'error: couldn't create a temp dir: No such file or directory (os error 2) at path /tmp/chump-binary-refresh-65988/target/release/deps/rustcA7kAs9'. Net: MISSION-012 deploy FAILS every time on this machine; binary stays stale. Repro today: 17:21Z and 17:29Z auto-deploy ticks both failed in 12 min with identical error. FIX: drop a .chump-no-reap sentinel file (stale-worktree-reaper.sh already honors it — see scripts/ops/active-target-reaper.sh:23 'Skip if .chump-no-reap exists') in /tmp/chump-binary-refresh-<PID>/ at the start of refresh-runner-binary.sh, before cargo build runs. 1-line fix.
