- id: RESILIENT-122
  domain: RESILIENT
  title: "RESILIENT: bot-merge wall-clock budget not enforced + no lease heartbeat during long ship"
  status: done
  priority: P1
  effort: m
  description: |
    2026-06-05: 'scripts/coord/bot-merge.sh --gap RESILIENT-103 --auto-merge' ran 21 minutes (pushed the branch but NEVER created the PR) with no self-abort, despite CHUMP_SUBAGENT_BOT_MERGE_BUDGET_S=900s (15min) being documented in CLAUDE.md + SUBAGENT_DISPATCH.md. Two defects: (a) the wall-clock budget is DOCUMENTED but NOT ENFORCED by bot-merge itself — nothing killed the 21-min run; the operator had to pkill it manually. (b) bot-merge does NOT heartbeat the gap lease during a long ship, so the lease expired (02:19:36) MID-SHIP, dropping the gap back to pickable and forcing a lease-less manual push+PR recovery. Net cost: 21min lost + manual recovery + expired lease + a confusing multi-process cleanup.
  acceptance_criteria:
    - bot-merge.sh self-aborts with a non-zero exit + clear message when it exceeds CHUMP_SUBAGENT_BOT_MERGE_BUDGET_S without hitting a progress marker (branch-pushed / PR-created), so a wedge cannot run unbounded
    - bot-merge heartbeats the gap lease (chump --heartbeat) at least once per N seconds during the ship so a long-but-progressing ship does not expire its own lease
    - on self-abort bot-merge emits kind=bot_merge_budget_exceeded to ambient.jsonl with elapsed + last-step, and prints the manual-fallback recipe (push + gh pr create + gh pr merge --auto) as its LAST output line so it survives a '
    - " tail' pipe"
    - regression test simulates a slow/stalled step and asserts the budget guard fires within the budget window
  notes: |
    MISSION-010 Gate0 substrate-self-heals. bot-merge-silent-wedge is the #1 wedge class (ship-assist playbook); this is the enforcement gap behind it.
