  priority: P1
  effort: xs
  acceptance_criteria:
    - "Reproducer: tail -100 .chump-locks/ambient.jsonl | python3 -c 'import sys,json; [json.loads(l) for l in sys.stdin if l.strip()]' raises JSONDecodeError on ~4% of lines"
    - "Identify the malformed emitters: scan ambient.jsonl for the broken lines, identify which kind/source produces them (likely a script using printf with un-escaped quotes in a field value, OR an emit pipe that's getting partially-written under concurrent writes)"
    - "Fix root cause: every ambient emitter must use a JSON-safe encoder (jq -c, python -c 'json.dumps()') NOT bare printf. Audit scripts/coord/broadcast.sh, scripts/coord/ambient_emit.sh, src/ambient_emit.rs, and any one-off printf '{\"ts\":...}' patterns for shell-quoting bugs"
    - "Add scripts/ci/test-ambient-jsonl-integrity.sh: scan last N lines of ambient.jsonl, fail if ANY line is not valid JSON. Run in CI on every push"
