- id: RESILIENT-138
  domain: RESILIENT
  title: "RESILIENT (Cut-Friction): chump claim must sync the gap YAML into the worktree — every fresh-gap ship hits bot-merge not-found until copied in"
  status: done
  priority: P1
  effort: m
  description: |
    Part of MISSION-044. A freshly reserved+claimed gap is NOT present in the worktree (docs/gaps/<ID>.yaml + state.db entry live only in the main checkout), so bot-merge preflight reports "not found in state.db" and wedges until the operator/agent manually copies the YAML + runs chump gap import. Hit on CREDIBLE-128, RESILIENT-133, and META-287 this session.
  acceptance_criteria:
    - after chump claim, docs/gaps/<ID>.yaml + the state.db entry exist in the worktree with no manual copy
    - OR bot-merge auto-imports the gap from the canonical store on not-found
    - a freshly reserved+claimed gap ships via bot-merge with no manual gap-def step
  notes: |
    RECONCILE: already shipped via PR #4013 (f41e25f6, "fix(RESILIENT-138):
    bot-merge defaults CHUMP_REPO to the main checkout"), which is on
    origin/main. Root cause: bare `chump` invocations inside bot-merge.sh
    (gap show/preflight/set/ship) resolve state.db via
    `repo_path::repo_root()`, which falls back to CWD when CHUMP_REPO/
    CHUMP_HOME are unset and no .env is found — in a linked worktree that
    CWD has no `.chump/state.db` of its own, so a freshly reserved+claimed
    gap reported "not found in state.db" until CHUMP_REPO was exported by
    hand. Fix: `export CHUMP_REPO="${CHUMP_REPO:-$MAIN_REPO}"`
    (scripts/coord/bot-merge.sh:1521), defaulting to MAIN_REPO (already
    resolved via --git-common-dir, correct regardless of env/.env state)
    right after sourcing repo-paths.sh, while still respecting an
    explicitly-set CHUMP_REPO. This satisfies AC bullet 2 (bot-merge
    transparently resolves state.db lookups to the canonical main-checkout
    store on a worktree-local miss) and therefore bullet 3 (a
    freshly reserved+claimed gap ships via bot-merge with no manual
    gap-def step). Two later duplicate attempts at the same fix
    (d3a394c5, 4967a8ff) exist on unmerged sibling branches from
    concurrent fleet claims of this gap; f41e25f6/#4013 is the one that
    landed on origin/main. Same reconcile pattern as RESILIENT-052
    (#4016), RESILIENT-081 (#4015), RESILIENT-218 (#4014).
  closed_date: '2026-08-20'
  closed_pr: 4013
  outcome_id: RESILIENT-000

