    2026-07-19 ~18:30 the operator got a macOS TCC prompt: 'chump' requesting iCloud Drive access. Mechanism: worker claude sessions run with the operator's full user file authority; a mid-gap broad find/grep strayed past the repo into an iCloud-synced location and macOS attributed it to the fleet parent. Operator denied (correct — nothing in the fleet needs iCloud). Structural fix: chumpd (MISSION-051) spawns every worker post-cutover and is the chokepoint to constrain the file view — sandbox-exec profile or equivalent allowing repo + claim worktrees + /tmp + toolchains, deny-by-default elsewhere; a denied stray becomes a logged event (kind exists via ambient), not a scary operator prompt. Interim: worker prompt discipline (search within repo paths only) is advisory-only and insufficient.
