  title: "RESILIENT: chump-binary-unwedge.sh uses gtimeout + BSD stat — false wedge diagnosis kills every ship on Linux hosts"
  status: done
  priority: P0
  effort: xs
  description: |
    scripts/dev/chump-binary-unwedge.sh probe uses gtimeout (homebrew-only name; absent on Linux → command-not-found → probe 'fails') and stat -f '%i' (BSD; on Linux returns multi-line filesystem info → garbage mv filename). Net effect on chumpd-eu: healthy binary falsely diagnosed as wedged, self-heal mv fails, bot-merge doctor preflight declares 'binary wedged, could not self-heal' and every free-tier ship dies (all EU cycles rc=1, 2026-07-22 05:45Z). Fix: portable timeout resolver (gtimeout||timeout) + GNU-first stat (stat -c '%i' || stat -f '%i').
  acceptance_criteria:
