  description: |
    fresh-eyes-loop.sh line ~151 (_brief_says_healthy) uses bash-4-only ${txt,,}. macOS system bash is 3.2, no homebrew bash installed, so the shebang #!/usr/bin/env bash resolves to 3.2 and throws 'bad substitution'. This kills comparators 1/4/5 (all call _brief_says_healthy) yet the loop still exits 1 (all-clear) — the mirror silently lies exactly the way fresh-eyes exists to catch. Found 2026-07-23 running 'run fresh look'; manual comparison found 2 real disagreements the tool hid (2 pr_stuck_cluster in 30min + SLO breach). Fix is a portable tr-based lowercase; grep for other ${var,,}/${var^^} bash-4-isms in the same file.
