    invoked via absolute path from a worktree (the normal pattern: cd /tmp/chump-X &&
    bash /Users/jeffadkins/Projects/Chump/scripts/coord/agent-dispatch-guardrail.sh),
    SCRIPT_DIR resolves to the MAIN repo's scripts/coord, so REPO_ROOT is always the
    main checkout, never the worktree the orchestrator actually cd'd into. Every
    branch/lease check silently validates against main's branch ("main") instead of
    the worktree's real branch (e.g. chump/credible-174-claim), producing a false
    BLOCKED on every worktree-based dispatch unless the caller happens to already
    know to set CHUMP_REPO_ROOT explicitly -- which nothing in
    docs/process/SUBAGENT_DISPATCH.md's usage example mentions.
    
    Workaround used: CHUMP_REPO_ROOT=/tmp/chump-<gap> bash .../agent-dispatch-guardrail.sh ...
  acceptance_criteria:
    - the guardrail auto-detects REPO_ROOT from the invoking shell's cwd (git rev-parse --show-toplevel from PWD) when CHUMP_REPO_ROOT is unset, instead of from the script's own file location
    - docs/process/SUBAGENT_DISPATCH.md's usage example is updated to show the correct invocation (either the auto-fix above, or an explicit CHUMP_REPO_ROOT= if auto-detect isn't the chosen fix)
    - "test: running the guardrail via its absolute path while cwd is a worktree correctly detects the worktree's branch, not main's"
