- id: RESILIENT-246
  domain: RESILIENT
  title: "RESILIENT: the curator has been dead 12 days and nothing noticed — chump's product-management layer exits 78 silently"
  status: done
  priority: P1
  effort: s
  description: |
    Two defects, and the second one matters more. (1) com.chump.curator-supervisor exits 78 every 600s and has since roughly 2026-07-26. Diagnose and fix the config error. (2) Nothing noticed for twelve days. The fleet has watchdogs for reapers (dev.chump.reaper-watchdog) and for PRs (bot-merge-watchdog, stale-pr-reaper) but no liveness check on the curator itself, and the fleet-brief does not report when the last curator action was. A silent PM layer is worse than an absent one because the absence is invisible: the brief printed ZERO-WASTE 0 pickable on 2026-08-07 without ever saying that the thing which fixes that has not run since July. Context: this sits inside a broader finding that 14+ of ~70 chump launchd jobs currently exit non-zero (127 command-not-found, 78 config, -15 SIGTERM). Fix this one on its own merits; the sweep is separate.
  acceptance_criteria:
    - com.chump.curator-supervisor exits 0 and completes a real pass — proven by a fresh .chump-locks/curator-* artifact dated after the fix, not merely by a clean exit code
    - last-curator-action age is surfaced where an operator already looks (fleet-brief line or the scoreboard), so a future silence is visible within one reporting cycle rather than twelve days
    - a liveness check fails loudly when the curator has not acted in N cycles, following the existing reaper-watchdog pattern rather than inventing a new one
    - the root cause of exit 78 is written down in the gap notes — a config error that recurs unexplained will recur
    - "regression: a test or check proves a curator that cannot start is reported, not silently skipped"
  notes: |
    [2026-08-09T17:06:33Z] ROOT CAUSE OF EXIT 78 (verified by experiment 2026-08-09, not inferred): the plist put a cargo build artifact directly in ProgramArguments — /Users/jeffadkins/Projects/Chump/target/release/chump-curator-supervisor. install-curator-supervisor.sh preferred ~/.cargo/bin/chump-curator-supervisor but that binary was never installed there (the fleet other six daemons are), so it fell through to the target/release fallback and baked a DISPOSABLE path into the plist. target/release is reclaimed by cargo clean, cargo-target-reaper, and disk-pressure reaps; around 2026-08-01 it was reclaimed and launchd could no longer spawn the job. launchd exit 78 = EX_CONFIG = cannot execute ProgramArguments[0]. Reproduced with a throwaway agent pointed at a nonexistent path: launchctl list showed "-  78  com.chump.r246probe" and BOTH log files were created and stayed EMPTY. That empty-log result IS the twelve-day outage: launchd fails before the process exists, so it never opens StandardOutPath/StandardErrorPath. curator-supervisor.out.log ends mid-stride at 2026-07-31T23:10 MDT with "all curators healthy" and nothing follows. No error to grep, no non-zero exit in any log. Silence was the entire symptom.
    [2026-08-09T17:06:48Z] WHY NOTHING NOTICED — three independent layers, all now closed or filed. (1) Nothing graded the curator: dev.chump.reaper-watchdog grades nine reaper/daemon heartbeats and the curator was not among them. (2) fleet-brief ALREADY KNEW and threw it away: the INFRA-2040 block walks every com/dev.chump.* label and collects non-zero exits into _sfd_dead_count, so it would have listed com.chump.curator-supervisor(exit=78) on EVERY run for twelve days — but the banner is gated `_merge_stale == 1 && _sfd_dead_count > 0` and _merge_stale requires no merge into main for 12h. Chump merges many times an hour, so that gate is ~never true and the dead-daemon list was computed then discarded. (3) The installer own check could not see it: is_loaded() matched ANY exit status, so --check reported "LOADED — running" for a job that had not run once in twelve days. Loaded was never health; exit 78 is loaded too. FIX: plist ProgramArguments is now /bin/bash + a version-controlled repo script (the dev.chump.reaper-watchdog shape) so launchd can always spawn it; scripts/ops/curator-supervisor-run.sh stamps the standard reaper heartbeat so the EXISTING reaper-heartbeat-watchdog grades curator-supervisor (no new mechanism); fleet-brief prints an UNCONDITIONAL Curator line; the installer installs to ~/.cargo/bin and refuses a target/-based plist. PR #3543. ALSO FOUND, filed separately: crates/chump-curator-supervisor/src/main.rs silent_stall_check returns Ok((false,None)) = healthy when a role has NEVER heartbeated — there are ZERO curator_heartbeat events in a 10MB ambient.jsonl, so the supervisor printed "all curators healthy" for the five days before it died while the curators had already stopped filing on 2026-07-26.
  closed_date: '2026-08-09'
  closed_pr: 3543
  outcome_id: RESILIENT-000
  evidence: |
    COMMAND: launchctl list | grep curator ; ls -lt .chump-locks/curator-*  |  OUTPUT: com.chump.curator-supervisor exits 78 (EX_CONFIG). Its most recent filed-work locks are dated Jul 25-26 2026 — curator-filed-balance_restock_ZERO-WASTE-2026-07-26, balance_restock_RESILIENT-2026-07-26, pr_unstick-2026-07-26 — and curator-sessions.json last written Jul 26 11:26. Today is Aug 7: twelve days of nothing, with no alert, no brief line, and no gap filed about it. Meanwhile the 2026-08-07 fleet-brief printed 'ZERO-WASTE 0 (!)' pickable — precisely the pillar-starvation condition the curator's balance_restock existed to correct.  |  THEORY: the curator is chump's product-management layer (pillar balance, PR unstick, backlog restock) and it is the only automated thing doing that job. It died of a config error five weeks after last being touched, and because nothing watches the watcher, the fleet has been running with no PM for twelve days. This is the reaper-watchdog pattern applied one level up: dev.chump.reaper-watchdog exists to notice dead reapers, and nothing plays that role for the curator. Exit 78 is deterministic, not flaky — it has failed every 600s for twelve days.  |  ALT: considered filing this as a plain bug on the curator — rejected as too narrow: the 12-day silence is the real defect, not the config error. A fixed curator that can die silently again returns us here. Considered rolling it into the 70-launchd-job audit — rejected: that audit is a big sweep and this is a live outage of a load-bearing organ; it should not wait behind a survey.

