  opened_date: '2026-08-19'
  outcome_id: MISSION-010

- id: RESILIENT-250
  domain: RESILIENT
  title: "DEADLOCK: gap-status-guard needs status=done before merge; PROOF-OF-MERGE needs the merge before done — PR #3499 stuck 24h"
  status: done
  priority: P1
  effort: s
  acceptance_criteria:
    - "OBSERVED CONSEQUENCE: PR #3499 (INFRA-1965) has been open since 2026-08-07T14:37Z with an expired lease and no path to merge. This deadlock is the reason, and it will silently hold any similar PR"
    - "WHY IT DOES NOT HIT EVERY PR — the asymmetry is the clue. gap-status-guard.yml:52-55 reads docs/gaps/<ID>.yaml only IF that file exists, and exits 0 with 'may be a new gap being filed' when it does not. Measured 2026-08-08: docs/gaps/INFRA-1965.yaml EXISTS (status: open) so #3499 is gated, while CREDIBLE-215 (#3510) and RESILIENT-248 (#3525) have NO per-file YAML and sail through the same gate. So the guard binds an arbitrary subset determined by which gaps happen to have a file checked in — it is not enforcing a policy, it is enforcing a filesystem accident"
    - "THE STEP NAME DOES NOT MATCH THE CODE. It is called 'Verify gap status flipped if PR title implies close', but gap-status-guard.yml:46 extracts ANY leading gap ID: grep -oE '^[A-Z]+-[0-9]+'. Nothing tests for close INTENT. And the pre-commit hook REQUIRES a gap ID in every commit subject, so by construction essentially every PR title 'implies close'. The condition the name promises was never implemented"
    - IT IS ALSO REDUNDANT, which is the strongest argument for fixing it in the guard rather than in chump gap ship. .github/workflows/auto-flip-on-merge.yml exists precisely to run 'chump gap ship <ID> --closed-pr <N> --update-yaml' AFTER the merge lands, and its header says it eliminates the silent-shipped-but-status-still-open backlog (31 gaps at the time). Post-merge flipping is already solved; requiring the flip PRE-merge duplicates it and creates the cycle
    - "PREFERRED FIX: make gap-status-guard non-blocking for the pre-merge case, or restrict it to titles that genuinely imply close, and let auto-flip-on-merge own the transition. Do NOT weaken INFRA-1392 PROOF-OF-MERGE — refusing to mark a gap done without evidence it merged is the honest half of this pair and exists to stop exactly the false done state"
    - WHATEVER THE FIX, PROVE IT ON A FIXTURE PR that has a checked-in docs/gaps/<ID>.yaml with status open, and assert it can reach merge. The bug is invisible on any gap lacking that file, which is why it survived
    - "ALSO RESOLVE THE 31-GAP QUESTION: if the guard is relaxed, confirm auto-flip-on-merge actually fires and closes the gap, otherwise the backlog it was built to kill comes back"
  closed_pr: 3556
  outcome_id: MISSION-010
  evidence: |
    COMMAND: chump gap ship INFRA-1965 --closed-pr 3499 --update-yaml | OUTPUT: 'INFRA-1392 PROOF-OF-MERGE: refusing to flip INFRA-1965 to status=done — no commit on local main carries this gap ID. Either (a) wait for the actual merge to land on main, or (b) ensure the merge commit subject mentions INFRA-1965.' AND the CI gate on the same PR: 'ERROR: PR title implies gap INFRA-1965 is closed, but status is open. Run: chump gap ship INFRA-1965 --closed-pr <PR-NUMBER> --update-yaml' — the gate prescribes exactly the command that PROOF-OF-MERGE refuses to run | THEORY: two guards, each individually correct, form a cycle. gap-status-guard.yml:65 fails the PR while status != done; INFRA-1392 refuses to set done without a commit on main; the commit cannot reach main because the PR cannot merge | ALT: considered and rejected — (a) the PR is simply red for other reasons: no, its other failures (FLEET-048, the merge conflict, the compile) are fixed and gap-status-check is what remains; (b) the operator forgot to bookkeep: no, the documented command is blocked by design; (c) it is specific to this gap: no, it is structural for any gap with a checked-in docs/gaps/<ID>.yaml

- id: RESILIENT-251
  domain: RESILIENT
  title: "RESILIENT: helsinki ran open to the internet — services bind 0.0.0.0 and depend on one iptables rule"
  status: done
  priority: P1
  effort: s
  description: |
    The exposure is closed; this gap is the defense-in-depth follow-through. Bind the three services to the Tailscale interface instead of every interface, so a future ufw mistake, flush, or reprovision does not silently re-expose them. Ollama: systemd drop-in with OLLAMA_HOST=100.101.188.30:11434 AND After=tailscaled.service + Wants=tailscaled.service, because binding a specific IP creates a boot-order dependency that will otherwise fail closed on reboot and take almanac's semantic layer down with it. NATS: same treatment for 4222/7422 via its config or unit. rerank_server.py on 8785 (root-owned, /root/rerank_server.py, almanac's cross-encoder): bind it to the tailscale ip too — and note it serves a feature almanac keeps DISABLED by default after measuring it negative, so retiring it is a legitimate alternative to hardening it. Each change verified from both sides before moving on: dark from the public ip, answering from the tailnet.
  acceptance_criteria:
    - ollama, nats (4222 and 7422) and 8785 each bind the Tailscale address rather than 0.0.0.0/*, confirmed by ss -lnt
    - each service has systemd ordering on tailscaled (After= and Wants=) so a reboot cannot leave it unable to bind — tested by an actual reboot or a tailscaled restart, not assumed
    - "after each change: verified DARK from the public ip AND verified ANSWERING from the tailnet, with the embedder specifically checked because almanac's semantic layer depends on it"
    - ufw remains enabled with the same allow-list; the firewall is not weakened on the assumption that binds are enough
    - 8785 is either bound to the tailnet or retired with a written reason, given the reranker is measured-negative and off by default
  notes: |
    DONE 2026-08-09 (completes the 2026-08-08 partial). NATS: rebound 0.0.0.0:4222/7422 -> 100.101.188.30 (both client port and leafnodes host) in /etc/nats/nats.conf. Blast-radius check before rebinding: grep'd every CHUMP_NATS_URL on-box -> /root/.chump/providers.env already points chumpd at a tailnet-style IP (not 127.0.0.1), local test scripts (test-a2a-layer1a-chaos.sh, test-integrator-stale-sla.sh) use their own ephemeral ports (14222/19999), not the shared 4222 broker, and the canonical installer (scripts/setup/nats-broker-install.sh) already defaults to tailnet-only bind — the 0.0.0.0 config on helsinki was drift from that intended design, not a deliberate choice. ss -tnp showed zero active connections at rebind time (chumpd/chump-reaper both inactive on this box right now), so there was nothing live to break. Systemd ordering was ALREADY present (/etc/systemd/system/nats.service.d/tailscale.conf, After+Wants=tailscaled.service) from the prior session — proved boot-order safety by restarting tailscaled: nats stayed active and re-bound to the tailnet IP. Verified both sides: dark from the public IP on 4222 and 7422 (raw /dev/tcp probe timed out), answering from the tailnet on both (INFO banner returned, auth_required:true, unauthenticated connect gets Authentication Timeout — auth stays as a second layer under the new bind). 8785 rerank_server.py: RETIRED per the gap's own AC5 alternative. It was never systemd-managed (a bare `python -u rerank_server.py` left running in a pts session since Jul26, no crontab/unit/rc.local entry) so it could not come back on reboot; killed both the shell wrapper and python pids. Confirmed port closed locally and dark from the public IP. It served almanac's cross-encoder rerank, which is measured-negative and OFF by default, so retiring beats hardening. ufw verified unchanged (default deny-in, 22/tcp + tailscale0 allow-list only) throughout — no bind change substituted for the firewall. Ollama's embedder path re-confirmed reachable over the tailnet (curl /api/tags returned the model list) as a smoke check that the almanac semantic layer's dependency chain is intact. All 5 AC now closed: (1) ollama+nats+8785 no longer bind 0.0.0.0 -- 8785 is gone, ollama+nats bind 100.101.188.30 only, per ss -lnt; (2) tailscaled ordering proven for both ollama (prior session) and nats (this session) via live tailscaled restart; (3) dark/answering verified both sides for all three, embedder specifically checked; (4) ufw untouched; (5) 8785 retired with reason.
  closed_date: '2026-08-09'
