- id: RESILIENT-265
  domain: RESILIENT
  title: "ask before you close: route the auto-closer through the approval system Chump already has (Discord buttons, resolver, timeout) instead of notify-then-destroy"
  status: done
  priority: P2
  effort: m
  acceptance_criteria:
    - BUILDS ON RESILIENT-263, which wired a one-way DM into the close path. This makes it two-way. Do NOT write a new approval mechanism — use src/approval_resolver.rs. Do NOT add a new messaging channel — use the Discord path already credentialed and proven (RESILIENT-263 delivered HTTP 200 twice)
    - "THE FLOW: before pr-failure-auto-rescue destroys an armed PR, call request_approval() to mint a request_id, DM the operator with approve/deny buttons whose custom_ids are exactly 'chump_approve:<id>' and 'chump_deny:<id>' (the handler at src/discord.rs:1210 already parses that prefix — match it exactly rather than inventing a scheme), then await the receiver with CHUMP_APPROVAL_TIMEOUT_SECS"
    - "THE MESSAGE MUST CARRY THE DECIDING FACT, not just the question: whether the red check is green on main right now. RESILIENT-263 already computes this at the close site. That single field is what separates 'this was a flake, keep it' from 'this is genuinely broken, close it' — and it is exactly what the operator had to work out by hand for PR #3510"
    - TIMEOUT MUST FAIL TO TODAY'S BEHAVIOUR, not hang. If no answer arrives, close as it does now and say in the close comment that the operator was asked and did not respond within N. A PR left in limbo forever because a phone was face-down is a worse failure than the one being fixed
    - "THE GATEWAY BOT IS THE ACTUAL BLOCKER and must be part of this gap or explicitly split out: the binary ships WITHOUT the discord feature (build shows --cfg feature=default; discord and telegram are optional) and no chump discord process is running. Buttons cannot be received until it is compiled in AND running under launchd with a liveness check — same lesson as the operator-recall handler, which has been enabled-but-dead since 2026-05-08 (RESILIENT-262)"
    - "AUTHORIZATION IS ALREADY HANDLED, do not weaken it: src/discord.rs:932/964/999 verifies msg.author.id.get() == CHUMP_READY_DM_USER_ID. Button interactions must enforce the same owner check — a custom_id is attacker-suppliable if anyone else can reach the bot, so never treat the id alone as authorization"
    - "SCOPE THE CONVERSATIONAL SURFACE DELIBERATELY: the gateway bot runs a FULL agent turn, so a DM that can command the fleet is an authorization surface. Reading and explaining may be conversational; any state-changing action must go through the fixed approve/deny buttons or a fixed verb set, so 'retry 3510' can never mean anything but one thing. Same lesson as holler's untrusted input"
    - "AND ANSWER UNRECOGNISED REPLIES: an unparsed DM must get 'I did not understand that — here is what I accept', never silence. Silent drops are how an operator learns the channel is one-way at the worst possible moment"
    - "VERIFY END TO END ON A REAL DEVICE: fixture PR, real DM, tap deny on the phone, assert the PR is NOT closed and the decision is recorded in ambient. A test that asserts request_approval() was called is exactly the mock-shaped green that let the operator-recall handler sit dead for three months"
