- id: RESILIENT-267
  domain: RESILIENT
  title: reaper's '0 commits ahead = merged' misread RECURRED — RESILIENT-099's fix only covered leased worktrees
  status: done
  priority: P1
  effort: s
  acceptance_criteria:
    - "The change described by \"reaper's '0 commits ahead = merged' misread RECURRED — RESILIENT-099's fix only covered leased worktrees\" is implemented in the relevant RESILIENT code path(s)."
    - At least one test (cargo test or scripts/ci/test-*.sh) proves the new behavior and fails without the change.
    - cargo fmt + clippy --all-targets -D warnings + check pass; no regression to existing tests.
  closed_date: '2026-08-09'
  closed_pr: 3546
  outcome_id: CREDIBLE-000
  evidence: |
    COMMAND: grep worktree_reaped .chump-locks/ambient.jsonl
    OUTPUT: {"ts":"2026-08-09T16:44:48Z","kind":"worktree_reaped","worktree":"/tmp/chump-r246",
      "reason":"branch merged into origin/main","branch":"resilient-246-curator"}
    Created ~35 min earlier by 'git worktree add -b resilient-246-curator main'; a session
    was actively editing it. Hit a SECOND time the same hour by another agent, independently.
    
    PRIOR ART I FAILED TO CHECK FIRST: RESILIENT-099 (status=done, 2026-06-05) is the same
    misreading — 'reaps an ACTIVELY-LEASED 0-commits-ahead worktree (misreads branch merged
    into origin/main)'. Its acceptance was scoped to 'active lease must hard-block reap', so
    the fix protected LEASED worktrees and left the root misreading in place. A worktree made
    by a bare 'git worktree add' holds no chump lease, so it inherited none of that protection.
    This is a RECURRENCE of a gap marked done, not a new discovery.
    
    THEORY: 'git merge-base --is-ancestor branch origin/main' answers TRUE for a branch with
    zero commits, because such a branch trivially IS an ancestor. Ancestry is not evidence of
    merging; it is the absence of divergence. RESILIENT-099 treated the symptom (protect the
    leased case) rather than the predicate.
    
    ALT rejected: extend lease coverage to every worktree. That keeps a false predicate and
    makes correctness depend on every creator remembering to take a lease — the same shape
    that failed here.
    
    STATUS: fix already merged in PR #3545 (branch_has_own_commits + a new-worktree grace
    window + 8 regression tests in scripts/ci/test-stale-worktree-reaper-empty-branch.sh).
    This gap exists to carry the correct ID: that PR cites RESILIENT-263, which is an
    UNRELATED gap (the operator escalation channel, PR #3544). I invented the number instead
    of reserving one. The wrong reference is on main and needs correcting.

