  notes: |
    [2026-08-10T02:05Z] Shipped as PR #3562, merged to main at 2026-08-10T01:59:45Z as e9101279 with 27/27 checks green. Verified on origin/main, not assumed: `git show origin/main:crates/chump-curator-supervisor/src/main.rs | grep -c 'NeverSeen|HeartbeatState|heartbeat_kind_for'` = 43 matches.
    
    THE FIX: silent_stall_check's bool became a four-state verdict (Fresh/Stalled/NeverSeen/Blind). Only Stalled is auto-remediated — a role that never started has no pane to respawn, and a scan that cannot cover its threshold window reports blindness rather than guessing. Heartbeat matching now accepts BOTH the generic curator_heartbeat kind and each productized role's own <role>_heartbeat kind, which is the defect that kept the fail-open invisible: the detector was subscribed to a channel no working curator publishes to. Window is no longer a fixed 500 lines (12.0 min at the measured 41.7 lines/min, against a 10-min threshold); coverage is proven per tick against the oldest observed timestamp, so the nightly ambient rotation yields one honest 'cannot see' instead of six false P0s. All-roles-never-started aggregates to ONE launcher-level gap with no restarts and no sub-agents.
    
    VERIFIED AGAINST LIVE AMBIENT (dry-run, three scenarios): nothing running -> 6 dead, ONE P0, no remediation. All six emitting their real kinds -> 'all 6 curators healthy', silent. Rotated 1 min ago -> one BLIND warning, zero gaps. 24 Rust unit tests (10 new) + the shell suite green.
    
    ALSO REPAIRED, same PR: scripts/ci/test-curator-supervisor.sh could not find its own binary (hardcoded $REPO_ROOT/target after CARGO_TARGET_DIR moved — built it, failed to locate it, exit 1 on main for everyone); seven 'grep -c ... || echo 0' counters where grep -c prints its count AND exits 1, making the value $'0\n0' and [[ -gt ]] a syntax error that bash reports before SKIPPING the assertion — the check that the circuit breaker suppresses sonnet spawns could never fail.
    
    STILL OPEN, deliberately not done here: the six curators are genuinely not running (tmux has no server). Starting them is six panes and six Opus sessions — an operator decision, not a side effect of a detector fix. This gap closes the lying, not the silence.
    
    FOLLOW-UPS FILED: RESILIENT-281 (the same grep -c pattern in 102 files, 74 feeding a numeric comparison). CREDIBLE-277 (EVENT_REGISTRY.yaml, the declared ground-truth contract, does not parse as YAML — pre-existing on main).
    
    PROCESS NOTE: RESILIENT-246's notes claimed this defect was 'filed separately'; no such gap existed. The filing was claimed, not done — which is why this one got a reserved ID and a receipt rather than a mention.
  closed_date: '2026-08-10'
  closed_pr: 3562
  outcome_id: MISSION-010
  evidence: |
    COMMAND: grep -c curator_heartbeat .chump-locks/ambient.jsonl{,.1,.2} ; grep -n '_heartbeat' scripts/coord/*-loop.sh ; tmux has-session -t chump-curators  |  OUTPUT: ZERO curator_heartbeat events across 30,783 retained ambient lines and three days (Aug 7-9); the four productized curators each emit their OWN kind instead — handoff_heartbeat, ci_audit_heartbeat, decompose_heartbeat (role='curator-opus-decompose', not 'decompose'), md_links_heartbeat; 'no server running' — the tmux session hosting all six curators does not exist. silent_stall_check returned Ok((false,None)) = HEALTHY for a role that had never heartbeated, and again when the ambient file was missing, under a comment claiming it would 'treat as stalled if file truly missing'. Its unit test asserted the fail-open: assert!(!stalled, 'no ambient file -> should not stall'). Third defect: the scan read a fixed 500 lines, which at the measured 41.7 lines/min covers 12.0 minutes against a 10-minute threshold.  |  THEORY: three defects that each hid the next. The name mismatch meant the detector was subscribed to a channel no working curator publishes to, so the fail-open had nothing to fail open on and the check read permanently green; the 500-line window meant that even after fixing both, a busier fleet would scroll a healthy heartbeat out of view. RESILIENT-246's notes say this was 'filed separately' but no such gap exists in the registry — the filing was claimed, not done.  |  ALT: considered fixing only the fail-open as RESILIENT-246's note proposed — rejected and PROVEN wrong by experiment: with the name mismatch left in place that change pages all four productized roles as dead on every tick while they run perfectly. Considered widening the 500-line window to a bigger constant — rejected: a window that must be re-tuned whenever the fleet gets chattier is not a check; coverage is now proven per tick against the oldest observed timestamp instead.

- id: RESILIENT-281
  domain: RESILIENT
  title: 74 shell assertions across the fleet silently skip on the zero case — 'grep -c ... || echo 0' yields the two-line string $'0\n0'
  status: blocked
  priority: P2
  effort: m
  acceptance_criteria:
    - "Zero occurrences of the 'grep -c ... "
    - ""
    - " echo 0' idiom remain under scripts/ — sweep command and its 0-file output pasted in the notes (baseline today: 102 files, 103 occurrences, 74 feeding a numeric comparison)"
    - At least one previously-DEAD assertion is demonstrated failing on a seeded bad input after the fix, proving the repaired assertions can actually fire — a silent conversion is not evidence
    - "Both failure directions are handled, not just one: '-gt 0'/-ge 1' sites (false PASS) AND '-eq 0' sites (false FAIL from the wrong branch)"
    - A pre-commit or CI guard rejects new instances of the idiom, and that guard has its own test that fails without it
    - Full scripts/ci suite run shows ZERO 'syntax error in expression' lines in output — a suite that prints a bash syntax error and then PASS is the bug, so absence of that string is the regression check
    - Per-site workarounds already patched around the symptom (e.g. fleet-brief.sh's '[[ -z $_subjects_24h ]] && ships_24h=0') are removed or justified, so the root fix is not layered on top of the band-aid
  notes: |
    [2026-08-29T02:02:35Z] INFRA-3832 auto-block: 3 consecutive non-ship cycles (last kind=rc=1, rc=1, cycle_log=0B). Worker kept re-picking + looping; blocked to leave the pick pool. Un-block after fixing the spec / decomposing.
  opened_date: '2026-08-19'
  outcome_id: MISSION-010
  evidence: |
    COMMAND: X=$(grep -c pat empty_file 2>/dev/null || echo 0); printf 'value=%q\n' "$X"; if [[ "$X" -gt 0 ]]; then echo FIRED; fi  |  OUTPUT: value=$'0\n0' and bash prints '[[: 0\n0: syntax error in expression (error token is "0")' then SKIPS the conditional. grep -c always prints its count AND exits 1 on no-match, so '|| echo 0' appends a SECOND line rather than substituting one. Static sweep of scripts/: 102 files, 103 occurrences, 74 of which feed a numeric comparison ([[ -gt/-lt/-eq/-ge/-le ]] or (( ))). Confirmed live in scripts/ci/test-curator-supervisor.sh, where the assertion that the RESILIENT-035 circuit breaker suppresses sonnet spawns could never fail — the test printed a bash syntax error and then 'PASS'. Fixed there in PR 3562; the other 101 files are untouched.  |  THEORY: the failure direction depends on the comparison, which is why it has survived. Where the test expects a nonzero count (-gt 0, -ge 1) the syntax error skips the assertion and the suite reports a false PASS. Where it expects zero (-eq 0) the error takes the else branch and reports a false FAIL. Both are silent: bash writes the syntax error to stderr and continues, so a green suite and a red suite can both be lying. scripts/dispatch/fleet-brief.sh already carries a per-site workaround ([[ -z "$_subjects_24h" ]] && ships_24h=0), which is evidence the bug has been hit and patched symptom-by-symptom rather than at the root.  |  ALT: considered a blanket sed across all 102 files in PR 3562 — rejected as unreviewable and out of scope for a curator fix; a 100-file mechanical sweep deserves its own diff and its own test. Considered adding a shellcheck rule — SC2126 is adjacent but does not cover this; a targeted pre-commit grep for 'grep -c.*|| echo' is the cheaper durable guard and should ship WITH the sweep so the pattern cannot return.

