- id: RESILIENT-381
  domain: RESILIENT
  title: pixel-worker.sh worktree base must default to $TMPDIR (Termux-writable), not hardcoded /tmp
  status: open
  priority: P2
  effort: xs
  description: |
    scripts/setup/pixel-worker.sh (repo-managed) hardcoded WORKTREE_BASE=/tmp, which is NOT app-writable on Android/Termux so chump claim fails with Permission denied. The live Pixel worker only runs via a hand-crank CHUMP_WORKTREE_BASE export; a node-setup regeneration of this repo file would wipe the hand-crank and break the worker. Fix: default to ${CHUMP_WORKTREE_BASE:-${TMPDIR:-/tmp}} so Termux (TMPDIR=$PREFIX/tmp) works out of the box and datacenter Linux (TMPDIR unset -> /tmp) is unchanged.
