- id: RESILIENT-408
  domain: RESILIENT
  title: "auto-deploy verifies wrong binary: gates on target/release, CJ workers exec ~/.cargo/bin/chump"
  status: done
  priority: P1
  effort: s
  description: |
    MISSION-012/RESILIENT-211 deploy lineage. The CJ auto-deploy organ (scripts/ops/auto-deploy.sh -> scripts/setup/refresh-runner-binary.sh) gates deploy success on TARGET_BIN=CHUMP_RUNNER_BIN=~/Projects/chump/target/release/chump, but the workers (cj-worker-run.sh) exec ~/.cargo/bin/chump (first in their PATH) — a different file/inode. Result: binary_auto_deployed is emitted and auto-deploy-last-sha.txt advanced while the running worker executes stale code (observed 2026-08-24 05:50: worker binary was the 04:49 build with 0 EFFECTIVE-465 markers though auto-deploy had reported success). This is the merged-not-running disease on the deploy side. Script-only change (express lane, skips cargo-test gate). Do NOT blind-edit CI/hook Rust core. Push with --no-verify.
  acceptance_criteria:
    - auto-deploy verifies the binary the fleet PATH actually resolves chump to (on Linux nodes, ~/.cargo/bin/chump when present) rather than hardcoding target/release/chump
    - After install, the deploy confirms the PATH-resolved binary build SHA == origin/main HEAD SHA (and carries the expected build marker when one is defined); on mismatch it emits kind=binary_auto_deploy_failed reason=worker_binary_sha_mismatch and exits non-zero
    - binary_auto_deployed is emitted and auto-deploy-last-sha.txt written ONLY after that post-install verification passes — never on an unverified or mismatched install
    - refresh-runner-binary.sh honors an externally-provided CARGO_TARGET_DIR (isolated build dir) instead of hard-overriding to REPO_ROOT/target, so the deploy build cannot lock-contend with worker builds
    - "a scripts/ci regression test asserts: a stale PATH-resolved binary after a refresh causes the deploy to exit non-zero and NOT emit binary_auto_deployed"
  notes: |
    [2026-08-24T15:55:17Z] Filed by CJ fleet engineer 2026-08-24 while landing EFFECTIVE-465. Companion finding: EFFECTIVE-465 restrict-tools-to-edit-only fires correctly in the running worker (marker present), but floor still empty-diffs on non-trivial gaps (model burns 8192-token budget post-restriction with no appliable str_replace); trivial one-line gaps (CREDIBLE-301) DO land on flash.
  closed_date: '2026-08-26'
  closed_pr: 4238
  outcome_id: MISSION-012
  evidence: |
    COMMAND: systemctl show chump-auto-deploy.service -p Environment; stat -c %i ~/.cargo/bin/chump ~/Projects/chump/target/release/chump. OUTPUT: CHUMP_RUNNER_BIN=target/release/chump (inode 2136728); worker wrapper PATH=~/.cargo/bin:...:target/release so chump resolves to ~/.cargo/bin/chump (inode 842125) — DIFFERENT file. At 05:50 worker binary was 04:49 build with 0 EFFECTIVE-465 markers while auto-deploy reported binary_auto_deployed. THEORY: auto-deploy.sh + refresh-runner-binary.sh gate success on TARGET_BIN=CHUMP_RUNNER_BIN=target/release/chump, NOT the artifact workers exec (~/.cargo/bin/chump, first in PATH) — deploy reports success while running worker stays stale = merged-not-running on deploy side. Compounded: refresh-runner-binary.sh hard-overrides CARGO_TARGET_DIR to REPO_ROOT/target (shared warm target workers build into), inviting lock contention. ALT: just repoint CHUMP_RUNNER_BIN — REJECTED: no fail-loud verification against PATH-resolved binary means drift silently recurs.

- id: RESILIENT-409
  domain: RESILIENT
  title: farmer gate must not RED-block free-tier/deepseek claims on stale Anthropic-oauth mtime (RESILIENT-069 self-strangle)
  status: done
  priority: P1
  effort: s
  acceptance_criteria:
    - "1) In src/farmer_status.rs check_oauth_fresh, when a free-tier cascade is configured (CHUMP_FREE_TIER_PROVIDERS non-empty), a stale ~/.chump/oauth-token.json mtime MUST NOT force oauth_fresh=false; fail-open with an explanatory reason. 2) Unit test: free-tier env + 33-day-old oauth-token.json + no fresh auth-status-cache => oauth_fresh true (GREEN). 3) Regression test: WITHOUT free-tier env, stale token still => RED (unchanged). 4) auth-status-cache rc!=0 BROKEN branch still forces RED even in free-tier mode (real auth failure not masked). 5) farmer status stays local-only, no network, <100ms."
  closed_date: '2026-08-26'
  closed_pr: 4260
  outcome_id: CREDIBLE-000
  evidence: |
    CJ fleet dark ~31.5h (0 merges since 2026-08-24T16:14Z). All 3 workers logged RESILIENT-069 farmer status RED every 60s. Root: check_oauth_fresh in src/farmer_status.rs falls through to ~/.chump/oauth-token.json mtime>3600s and RETURNS RED, but the execute-gap floor uses the free-tier deepseek cascade (CHUMP_FREE_TIER_PROVIDERS) and never uses the Anthropic oauth token — auth-status.sh returns GREEN. The oauth refresher (install-oauth-refresh-launchd.sh) is macOS-launchd-only so the token file is perpetually stale on Linux/CJ. Recurs every ~OAUTH_TOKEN_MAX_AGE_S. Receipt: fresh chump farmer status under worker env = GREEN once token touched; RED returns ~48min later as mtime re-crosses 3600s.

