- id: SYSTEM-CURATOR-ROUTINE
  title: Opus Curator — fleet health audit + decisions
  status: perpetual
  priority: P0
  effort: m
  description: |
    Proactive fleet health audit + curator decision-making (INFRA-789).
    
    Audit phase:
    1. chump health --slo-check (SLO breach detection)
    2. chump waste-tally --window 2h (cost + efficiency)
    3. chump gap audit-priorities --json (P0 inflation, vague gaps)
    4. Scan open PRs (detect stalls > 2h, failing checks)
    5. Validate pillar balance (each pillar has 2+ pickable xs|s|m gaps)
    
    Decision phase:
    1. If P0 > 5: demote 1-2 to P1 (inflation control)
    2. If vague pickable gaps exist: add concrete AC immediately
    3. If any pillar < 2 pickable: file gaps from ROADMAP.md
    4. If pr_stuck cluster (3+ in 2h): flag for unsticking + rebase
    5. If waste > 20%: file INFRA gap for root cause
    
    Output: all decisions + metrics logged to ambient.jsonl.

- id: SYSTEM-FAST-PATH-CHECK
  title: Emergency Fast-Path — fleet_wedge + silent_agent detection
  status: perpetual
  priority: P0
  effort: s
  description: |
    High-confidence signal detection for fleet emergencies (INFRA-789).
    
    Checks:
    1. fleet_wedge event → auto-scale fleet to 2 workers + invoke Opus for CI root-cause
    2. silent_agent_cluster (2+ in 1h) → invoke Opus to diagnose picker/lease bug
    
    State tracking (fleet-state.json):
    - Tracks wedged status, wedge_start, wedge_escalated
    - Implements back-off rules per CLAUDE.md scaling gate
    - Escalates after 30m of wedge persistence
    
    All other signals defer to curator (runs every 10m).

